    benchmark_summary: "Templar, built by Covenant Labs (covenant.ai, GitHub org one-covenant), is a decentralised pre-training protocol: miners train a shared model over commodity internet links and validators score the usefulness of submitted pseudo-gradients, using the team's own SparseLoCo/CCLoco compression. Its headline deliverable is real and shipped \u2014 Covenant-72B, a 72B-parameter LLM pre-trained with permissionless peers over the internet, with a technical report on arXiv and a free public chat interface at tplr.ai/chat. The team also publishes genuine research (PULSELoCo, PULSE weight-update sparsity, SparseLoCo) with named academic co-authors. CRITICAL CURRENT STATE: the repo README declares the protocol dormant \u2014 \"Templar is dormant. The Covenant-72B training run is complete... Templar's decentralized training protocol is not currently active, but may return in the future. Subnet 3 is now running Crusades, an MFU optimization competition on the same subnet (netuid 3) but with a different mechanism.\" Crusades is a tournament where miners host a train.py at a URL, commit it timelock-encrypted on chain, and validators execute it in a container and score median MFU. Live today: the free Covenant-72B chat, the public training dashboard (currently showing TEST_RUN_002, llama-8b, dense), public W&B and Grafana metrics, and the research corpus. Nothing is sold. AUDIT: Best decentralisation and engineering posture of the four, but with a live governance question. The main repo is MIT-licensed, has 158 stars, 58 forks and 25 contributors with genuinely distributed authorship (distributedstatemachine 866 commits, joellidin 851, epappas 250, AlexanderLavelle 190, noaonoszko 71, Quentin-Anthony 33) \u2014 this is real collaborative work, in no way a template fork. Verifiability is unusually strong: public Weights & Biases dashboard (wandb.ai/tplr/templar), public Grafana eval metrics (grafana.tplr.ai), CI with Codecov, and peer-reviewable arXiv papers. The team is doxxed and academically credentialed (Joel Lidin, Amir Sarfi, Erfan Miahi, Quentin Anthony, Evangelos Pappas, Benjamin Therien, Eugene Belilovsky, Samuel Dare). RED FLAG: the on-chain subnet identity is a placeholder that has never been cleaned up \u2014 subnet_name \"deprecated\", github_repo \"https://github.com/username/repo\", contact \"deprecated@gmail.com\", url \"www.deprecated.com\". Anyone reading the chain alone would conclude SN3 is dead. Covenant Labs controls the dominant validator, the training coordinator, the S3/R2 gradient buckets and the campaign definitions; a single org effectively decides what SN3 trains. No third-party security audit found. CAVEATS: The supplied name \"Templar\" is half-stale and I flagged rather than inherited it: Templar the protocol is self-declared DORMANT and netuid 3 has switched to the Crusades mechanism. Worse, BOTH codebases look idle \u2014 one-covenant/templar last pushed 31 March 2026 (and that commit was only a README update; the last substantive commit is 21 January 2026), and one-covenant/crusades last pushed 5 April 2026. That is over four months of no code on the mechanism supposedly running the subnet, while the sibling repo basilica was actively pushed through 28 July 2026 \u2014 so the org is alive but SN3 specifically is not where the work is going. I could NOT reconcile this with the dashboard showing TEST_RUN_002 \"Now Running\": I could not find the API or data source behind that panel and cannot confirm it is live rather than a stale static render, so treat \"a training run is currently active\" as unverified. tplr.ai/crusades returns 404 even though it is in the site nav \u2014 the Crusades surface is broken or unbuilt. Claim I consider overstated: the site's present-tense \"Incentivized Internet-wide AI training\" positioning, which the repo's own dormancy banner contradicts. I scored 55, not higher: the shipped 72B model and the research are genuinely top-decile for Bittensor, but score must reflect what the subnet does TODAY, and today SN3's mechanism has no visible development and no revenue. is_active is true \u2014 $25.8M market cap, 0.034% emission, and a live org \u2014 but this is a subnet in between mechanisms, and that transition is the single biggest risk to the emission stream.",
    active_users: "Actively checked tplr.ai, tplr.ai/chat, tplr.ai/dashboard, tplr.ai/research, covenant.ai and all 37 repos in github.com/one-covenant: there is no pricing page, no checkout, no API key issuance, no enterprise/contact-sales funnel and no billing code anywhere in the public surface. The Covenant-72B chat at https://www.tplr.ai/chat is free and unauthenticated. This is a research subnet whose output is models and papers, not a commercial product \u2014 pre-revenue by design, not by failure. Note: Covenant's OTHER subnet, Basilica (SN39), does sell compute; that is a different netuid and its economics must not be attributed to SN3.",
