    cost_saving_pct: 60,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "SN5 (formerly OpenKaito, transferred by Kaito to Latent Holdings in May 2025 and relaunched as Hone in August 2025) is run by Manifold Labs with Latent Holdings. Its actual on-chain mechanism today is an ARC-AGI-2 benchmark competition: miners expose an /info endpoint pointing at a git repo, validators submit that repo to a Sandbox Runner which builds it, runs prep with internet then inference network-isolated, and scores exact_match_rate. A 20% accuracy floor applies, top 5 miners above the floor get rewards on an exponential decay, and if nobody clears the floor 100% of emission is burned. Chain activity is real and heavy \u2014 242 of 256 neurons earn incentive, 11 validators, ~5.3 TAO/day recycled into registrations. There is no product a customer can buy; their own roadmap puts API deployment at 2027+. AUDIT: Open source under manifold-inc (hone, hone-api, hone-dashboard), plus Latent's broad Bittensor OSS footprint (developer-docs, subtensor, bt-decode). No third-party audit found. Sandbox design is sound on paper \u2014 miner inference runs without network access, submissions cached by repo+branch+commit, daily submission limits. But there is a hard centralisation dependency: scoring is not done by validators locally, it is delegated to a Sandbox Runner service, and the reward path also runs through the team's hone-api. Contributor concentration is extreme \u2014 the main repo has 3 contributors total (camfairchild of Latent, robertalanm of Manifold, one other). Effective control of the subnet's direction sits with two closely-allied private companies, Manifold Labs and Latent Holdings, who also run SN4 Targon and SN14 TaoHash. CAVEATS: Two things here should worry a buyer and neither is disclosed by the project. First, development has stopped: manifold-inc/hone has had ZERO commits since 2026-02-01 (last commit 2026-01-29 by Cameron Fairchild); hone-api last commit 2026-05-02, hone-dashboard 2026-04-28. That is roughly three to six months of silence on a subnet whose thesis is active research. Second, their own live dashboard is broken \u2014 https://www.hone.training/network returns 'API unreachable / Cannot reach hone-api', and reports Subnet 5 with 0 of 0 miners online and 0 validators, which flatly contradicts the 242 miners actually earning on chain. Third, the marketing and the code disagree about what this even is: the website describes a peer-to-peer distributed LLM training network, while the repo README describes an ARC-AGI-2 benchmarking subnet. I treat the website copy as stale and the ARC benchmark as the real mechanism, but I could not fully reconcile them. The ARC-AGI-2 ~85% target is an aspiration with no published progress. I cut the prior benchmark_score of 72 to 45: the on-chain mechanism runs and attracts miners, but the codebase is stalled, the public product surface is broken, and there is nothing to sell.",
    active_users: "No product, no pricing page, no API, no customers. hone.training sells only the research narrative ('large language models trained by the many, owned by no one'). Their published roadmap defers any commercial API to Phase 3, 2027+ \u2014 see the Phase 3 description 'transitioning to API deployment for decentralized access' at https://subnetalpha.ai/subnet/hone/. Zero external revenue.",
