    cost_saving_pct: 90,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "IOTA (Incentivised Orchestrated Training Architecture), by Macrocosmos, is decentralised LLM pretraining across the open internet. It replaced SN9's original winner-takes-all design \u2014 where every miner had to fit a whole model locally and hoarded weights \u2014 with a data- and pipeline-parallel SWARM in which model layers are distributed across heterogeneous, unreliable, adversarial nodes, so no participant holds the full model. Live on mainnet since 2 June 2025. The headline verifiable output is Project Orion / Orion-100B: a 100-billion-parameter model pretrained across globally distributed GPUs at roughly 65% of datacenter training efficiency, >30% model FLOP utilisation, with activation compression cutting inter-stage transfers from ~140MB to 2.2MB, run as 16 pipeline-parallel stages across three replicas over ~15 trillion tokens and 700+ experiments; they scaled from 1.5B to 100B params in about a month by April 2026. Shipped tooling: a miners dashboard, relaunched leaderboards, public auditor-payout endpoints that expose why specific compute was allocated to a run, and a 'Train at Home' desktop app that lets consumer hardware join and earn. What is NOT live: there is no product sold off the back of this \u2014 no inference API, no pricing page, no announced model licence or commercial release of Orion-100B. Permissionless participation on fully consumer-grade hardware (RTX 4090s, Apple Silicon) is explicitly stated as roadmap, not current. AUDIT: Current code is https://github.com/macrocosm-os/iota \u2014 created 2025-05-30, 9 contributors, 30 stars, 22 forks, at v4.9.2, last push 2026-07-31. Genuine original work led by named, public researchers (Steffen Cruz), backed by a peer-reviewable technical primer (arXiv 2507.17766) and a whitepaper. Two flags: the repo declares NO LICENSE, so there is no grant of rights to fork or build on it; and the legacy repo macrocosm-os/pretraining IS a fork, is dead (last push 2025-05-28, final commits literally 'Burn Emissions'), and should not be cited as this subnet's active codebase \u2014 anything on file pointing there is stale. Decentralisation is the weakest part of the story relative to the marketing: IOTA is architecturally built around a Macrocosmos-operated orchestrator that assigns layers, routes activations and coordinates the swarm, which is a genuine single point of failure sitting at the centre of a system sold as trustless. Macrocosmos is also subnet owner (18% cut) and the dominant validator/dev. The auditor payout endpoints are a real, unusual transparency positive. No third-party security audit found. CAVEATS: Could not independently verify the Orion-100B performance claims \u2014 the 65%-of-datacenter-efficiency and >30% MFU figures are self-reported by Macrocosmos with no external benchmark or third-party reproduction, and I found no published eval of the resulting model against open baselines. Could not verify current live training state: iota.macrocosmos.ai is JS-rendered and I could not reach a status API to confirm active miner count or whether a run is in progress right now. Could not establish any commercialisation path or timeline for the trained models. The existing recorded score of 65 is a few points high \u2014 the technology and team are strong, but a 65 implies more than 'impressive research with no product', and the orchestrator centralisation plus the missing repo licence both deserve to cost it. The existing $0 revenue is correct, and should be upgraded from an assumption to confirmed_pre_revenue. Overstated on their own materials: 'permissionless, accessible' framing understates how much the orchestrator is a central coordinator, and consumer-hardware participation is marketed alongside a system that in practice ran on A100s.",
    active_users: "Actively looked and found no product to buy. There is no pricing page, no API, no paid tier and no commercial offering attached to SN9 anywhere \u2014 I grepped the entire Macrocosmos documentation corpus (https://docs.macrocosmos.ai/llms-full.txt, 227KB) for pricing/credits/revenue/customer terms: every commercial hit belongs to Gravity / SN13 Data Universe (card on file, $5 free credits, pay-as-you-go plans at app.macrocosmos.ai), never to SN9. The SN9 docs describe only mining, validating, dashboards and the Train-at-Home app \u2014 money flows OUT to compute providers via the auditor payout system, not in. Orion-100B is presented as a research demonstration of viability, not a sold artefact. SN9 does not appear in any 2026 Bittensor revenue ranking I checked.",
    annual_revenue_usd: 0,
    revenue_confidence: "confirmed_pre_revenue",
    revenue_evidence: "Actively looked and found no product to buy. There is no pricing page, no API, no paid tier and no commercial offering attached to SN9 anywhere \u2014 I grepped the entire Macrocosmos documentation corpus (https://docs.macrocosmos.ai/llms-full.txt, 227KB) for pricing/credits/revenue/customer terms: every commercial hit belongs to Gravity / SN13 Data Universe (card on file, $5 free credits, pay-as-you-go plans at app.macrocosmos.ai), never to SN9. The SN9 docs describe only mining, validating, dashboards and the Train-at-Home app \u2014 money flows OUT to compute providers via the auditor payout system, not in. Orion-100B is presented as a research demonstration of viability, not a sold artefact. SN9 does not appear in any 2026 Bittensor revenue ranking I checked.",
    last_updated: "2026-08-12",
    sources: ["https://docs.macrocosmos.ai/subnets/subnet-9-iota", "https://docs.macrocosmos.ai/llms-full.txt", "https://iota.macrocosmos.ai", "https://github.com/macrocosm-os/iota", "https://github.com/macrocosm-os/pretraining", "https://arxiv.org/html/2507.17766v1", "https://www.macrocosmos.ai/research/iota_primer.pdf", "https://www.tao.media/macrocosmos-unveils-orion-100b-a-100b-parameter-distributed-ai-training-run/", "https://www.macrocosmos.ai/", "https://discord.gg/vRTaAXpRcd"],
