    subnet_id: 10,
    subnet_name: "Pareton",
    benchmark_score: 41,
    benchmark_category: "AI Inference",
    vs_provider: "Baseten (also Fireworks AI, Together AI, Databricks \u2014 managed inference optimisation)",
    cost_saving_pct: 0,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Pareton (netuid 10, a recent takeover of the slot \u2014 the GitHub org was only created 28 June 2026) runs inference-optimisation campaigns. A campaign pins a baseline vLLM commit, a base image digest, a GPU SKU, allowed/denied file globs and a content-addressed workload trace; miners author a git patch against that baseline, upload it via Pareton-presigned S3 and commit campaign_id/baseline_commit/patch_hash/retrieval_url on chain; a Pareton worker fetches the patch, runs four validation gates (identity, integrity, base-apply, surface), builds it hermetically inside the pinned image, pushes a content-addressed engine image to GHCR, and benchmarks correctness, a perf screen and SLA gates. Accepted improvements become the new baseline. The intended buyer is an enterprise running production inference who supplies a workload profile and SLA gates and pays for GPU-hours saved. Live today: a public docs site, a public dashboard listing campaigns, and a working Stage-0 REST API at api.pareton.ai (/v1/campaigns, /v1/stats, submissions and build-log endpoints). Roadmap / not live: essentially the whole product \u2014 pareton.ai states \"Build in progress \u00b7 Coming soon\", the README concedes \"On-chain scoring is still design-only\", and the bench harness still ships a --mock-bench path. AUDIT: Apache-2.0 licensed, code is public and is real original work \u2014 not a template fork \u2014 but authorship is dangerously concentrated: xavierlyu has 284 of ~291 commits on the main repo, with Danbog32 (5), fury0928 (1) and atosonik (1) as the only others. Bus factor of one. Architecturally the subnet is highly centralised by design and a buyer should understand this: Pareton operates the worker job loop, the hermetic builder, the GHCR image registry, the presigned S3 uploads, the Neon database, the GPU pod rental, and the campaign manifests \u2014 miners only submit patches. Validators do not independently verify benchmark results today because, per the README, on-chain scoring is design-only. That means the emission-relevant scoring path currently runs through Pareton's own infrastructure. There is no Pareton Discord \u2014 the README's Discord badge and link both point at the generic discord.gg/bittensor server, so there is no dedicated community channel. Team is partially identified (Xavier Lyu, contact xavier@pareton.ai; commits also from Bohdan Podziubanch) but there is no team page, company entity or funding disclosure. No third-party audit. On-chain identity is well-formed (correct repo, url, description). CAVEATS: The most important finding is a hard number that contradicts the surface impression of momentum. Their own API at https://api.pareton.ai/v1/stats returns 3 campaigns (1 open, 2 draft) and submissions total 3, with by_latest_state showing rejected: 3 and ZERO in every other state \u2014 no submission has ever been built, benchmarked or scored. Further, the campaigns are synthetic, not customer workloads: one campaign's workload_trace_url is literally \"file:///Users/xavierlu/Desktop/pareton/fixtures/campaigns/synthetic_v1/workload_trace.json\" (a path on the founder's laptop) and the other two point at S3 keys under \"stage0/campaigns/synthet...\". The dashboard campaign detail page also failed to load (\"Temporarily unavailable\"). So the \"open campaign on GLM-5.2-FP8 / H200\" that looks like production activity is a synthetic fixture with no valid miner submissions. AlphaGap's own feed describes Pareton as \"solid infrastructure shipping\" and \"undervalued\" \u2014 that read is based purely on commit velocity and is not supported by the traction data; do not inherit it. What IS genuine: commit activity is high and current (merged PRs on 11-12 August 2026, the day of research), the code quality signals are good (testnet CI, reproducible builds, gate design), and docs are unusually thorough for a subnet this young. Could not verify: any customer conversation, any funding, team size, or whether any GPU bench has ever run on real hardware rather than --mock-bench. Score 41 reflects competent early engineering with essentially zero validated network activity and no product.",
    active_users: "Their own marketing site states the product is not shipped: https://pareton.ai \u2014 \"Build in progress \u00b7 Coming soon\", with the only conversion path being an email address (xavier@pareton.ai). No pricing page, no checkout, no customer logos, no case studies. Corroborated from their live API: https://api.pareton.ai/health returns {\"ok\":true,\"service\":\"pareton\",\"stage\":0} and the OpenAPI description reads \"Stage 0 campaign + submission surface (SN10)\". This is a clear, evidenced pre-revenue state, not an unknown.",
    annual_revenue_usd: 0,
    revenue_confidence: "confirmed_pre_revenue",
    revenue_evidence: "Their own marketing site states the product is not shipped: https://pareton.ai \u2014 \"Build in progress \u00b7 Coming soon\", with the only conversion path being an email address (xavier@pareton.ai). No pricing page, no checkout, no customer logos, no case studies. Corroborated from their live API: https://api.pareton.ai/health returns {\"ok\":true,\"service\":\"pareton\",\"stage\":0} and the OpenAPI description reads \"Stage 0 campaign + submission surface (SN10)\". This is a clear, evidenced pre-revenue state, not an unknown.",
    last_updated: "2026-08-12",
    sources: ["https://pareton.ai", "https://pareton.ai/dashboard", "https://pareton.ai/docs", "https://api.pareton.ai/health", "https://api.pareton.ai/openapi.json", "https://api.pareton.ai/v1/stats", "https://api.pareton.ai/v1/campaigns", "https://github.com/Pareton-ai/pareton", "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Pareton-ai/pareton/main/README.md", "https://api.github.com/repos/Pareton-ai/pareton/contributors", "https://www.pareton.ai/", "https://discord.gg/bittensor (no dedicated server \u2014 README links the generic Bittensor Discord)"],
