    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. INACTIVE \u2014 parked, deregistered or abandoned.",
    benchmark_summary: "Mainframe (formerly Protein Folding) was Macrocosmos' decentralised-science subnet: miners ran protein molecular-dynamics simulations via OpenMM/GROMACS and protein-ligand docking via DiffDock, with a stated roadmap into DFT and other life-science compute. Its on-chain identity still describes hundreds of thousands of completed folding jobs since a June 2024 launch and a partnership with Rowan Scientific. However, the operator has wound the subnet down: the repo macrocosm-os/mainframe has had no commit since 2025-09-29 (10.5 months) while Macrocosmos pushes daily to apex, iota and data-universe; Macrocosmos deleted the SN25 documentation from its GitBook on 2026-05-20 (commit 'GITBOOK-623: Delete Sn37 + 25 docs'); and macrocosmos.ai no longer mentions Mainframe anywhere, listing only SN1 Apex, SN9 IOTA and SN13 Data Universe. On-chain the subnet now runs incentive_burn = 1.0 (100% of miner incentive burned) with exactly 1 active miner out of 256 keys. The app link in the README (app.macrocosmos.ai/mainframe) now bounces to a Macrocosmos Cloud login error page. Nothing is live and usable today. AUDIT: Code is open source under MIT (macrocosm-os/mainframe, 13 contributors, 31 stars) but frozen since 2025-09-29. Subnet owner coldkey and owner hotkey are the same key (5F6aRdsBHajN2NhZHBTB6ibBFu7YuZZEWruWzB8x6B6GiZ4D), still registered to Macrocosmos (contact brian@macrocosmos.ai). No third-party audit found. The dominant risk is not decentralisation but operator abandonment: a single company controls the subnet, has removed its docs and website presence, and set 100% incentive burn \u2014 the token can persist indefinitely as a shell while no work is performed. The 14 'active validators' are registered keys, not evidence of production work. CAVEATS: I could not inspect app.macrocosmos.ai/mainframe because it is behind a Macrocosmos Cloud login, so I cannot fully exclude a private/enterprise deployment still serving a customer. Web search was unavailable this session, so I could not find a formal sunset announcement, a Macrocosmos blog post, or X statements confirming the wind-down \u2014 the conclusion is inferred from repo history, docs deletion, website removal and on-chain burn state, which are individually strong and jointly conclusive. The on-chain identity summary (folding jobs, Rowan partnership) is operator-written marketing and is stale \u2014 treat it as a historical claim, not current status. The existing AlphaGap score of 63 and 'last researched 2026-04-07' predate the 2026-05-20 docs deletion and are now clearly wrong.",
    active_users: "No paid product exists to generate revenue. Macrocosmos removed all SN25 documentation (https://github.com/macrocosm-os/macrocosmos-content commit 2026-05-20 'GITBOOK-623: Delete Sn37 + 25 docs') and SN25 no longer appears on https://www.macrocosmos.ai/ or https://docs.macrocosmos.ai/. The subnet runs 100% incentive burn with 1 active miner, so no work is being produced or sold. Note Macrocosmos as a company does monetise SN13/Gravity \u2014 that revenue is NOT attributable to SN25.",
