    vs_provider: "Scale AI / Surge AI / Appen and other centralised LLM training-data vendors",
    cost_saving_pct: 0,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Orion is a data-mining subnet run by SILX Labs that produces LLM training datasets to spec. An orchestrator publishes signed 'campaigns' and per-miner assignments; miners turn assigned source data into model-ready datasets scored against a hosted judge plus a locally-run Quasar model; validators replay a hidden sample and set weights. The current campaign covers coding, mathematics, technical data and general knowledge. SILX's own Quasar long-context model is named as 'the first consumer' of the output, so today this is largely an internal data pipeline feeding the team's own model rather than an external product. The team is real and has shipped independently verifiable artefacts: the HuggingFace org silx-ai is verified and hosts six Quasar models (Quasar-10B at ~4.2k downloads / 52 likes, Quasar-Preview at ~1.3k downloads / 95 likes). The subnet itself, however, is explicitly at pilot stage \u2014 the mainnet storage prefix is literally 'orion/sn27-mainnet-pilot-001'. There is no buyer-facing product, no data marketplace UI, and no way for an outside customer to purchase a dataset today. AUDIT: Source is public on GitHub (SILX-LABS/Orion) but carries NO license file, so it is source-available rather than formally open source \u2014 a real consideration for anyone forking or relying on it. No third-party audit found. Decentralisation is weak by design and the README says so plainly: a single orchestrator, run by the subnet operator from 'one private launch configuration', publishes all campaigns and assignments and issues scoped storage grants; a single hardcoded publisher key (5H6Bqkzj...MqtX1mQw) signs campaigns; and all data flows through one operator-controlled AWS S3 bucket (orion-mainnet-979769297074-eu-central-1, eu-central-1). If the operator stops running the orchestrator, the subnet produces nothing. There is also an external dependency: both miner and validator require a CHUTES_API_KEY, so the pipeline relies on a third-party inference provider. Key-man risk is severe \u2014 the repo has exactly 1 contributor (ahmed3520) with 21 commits. Chain state: 256 active keys and 15 active validators but only 1 active miner, and zero emission at the snapshot block. CAVEATS: Could NOT verify: any revenue, any external customer, dataset volume actually produced, or whether the pilot has advanced past its first campaign. The Orion repo was created 2026-07-10 and last pushed 2026-07-24 \u2014 roughly three weeks stale at time of research \u2014 so I could not confirm the subnet is still being actively developed as opposed to paused. I could not check the team's X presence (no API key available here). IMPORTANT DISAMBIGUATION for anyone repeating this research: silx.ai is NOT this team \u2014 it resolves to 'Silex', an unrelated AI-native power/energy development company. The real SILX Labs footprint is the GitHub org SILX-LABS and the verified HuggingFace org silx-ai. Do not cite silx.ai as their website. Overstated: on-chain identity markets Orion as a subnet that 'discovers, generates, and curates high-quality training data for LLMs', which reads as a live data marketplace; in reality it is a single-campaign pilot whose only named consumer is the team's own model. Prior AlphaGap record had a hand-written profile calling it a data subnet with 'a planned commercial data product' \u2014 that framing is still accurate, and the prior score of 38 was close to right; I raised it only marginally on the strength of the verifiable HuggingFace artefacts.",
    active_users: "No pricing page, no customer-facing purchase path, and no disclosed figure exists. The strongest counter-signal is in their own code: the README at https://github.com/SILX-LABS/Orion documents an orchestrator that 'advances customer orders' and an '--execute-paid-canary' launch flag, showing a commercial flow is designed and partially built. But the deployment is labelled 'sn27-mainnet-pilot-001' (pilot), on-chain shows only 1 active miner, and no order volume, price per token/record, or customer is disclosed anywhere. Nothing to derive an estimate from.",
