    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "BitMind runs an adversarial deepfake/AI-generated-media detection network: one side of the subnet generates progressively harder synthetic images and video, the other trains detectors against it, so the detector retrains continuously against the moving generative frontier rather than being trained once and frozen. Live and usable today: a free web detector at bitmind.ai, a Chrome extension, native mobile apps, a public REST API with a free tier and a paid $100/mo Pro tier, and an MCP server. They published a technical paper (BitMind Forensics / BMF) in Jul 2026 claiming it matches or beats the strongest published detectors across 19 public benchmark datasets zero-shot, which the Opentensor account amplified. Buyers targeted are financial services, identity providers, government and platforms. Self-disclosed scale: 'millions of detection requests a month' (Aug 2026), with YouTube the single largest source of inbound detection requests. Enterprise licensing and on-prem deployment are advertised but no customer has been named. Repo is genuine research/infra work (bitmind-subnet, MIT, plus gasbench), though contributor count is small. AUDIT: Subnet code is open source under MIT (github.com/BitMind-AI/bitmind-subnet) with an active benchmarking repo (gasbench), but only 5 contributors and effectively two dominant committers \u2014 meaningful bus-factor risk. The commercial surface (bitmind.ai API, web detector, extension, mobile apps) is closed source and entirely BitMind-operated: a single point of failure for every customer-facing product and the sole billing path. Subnet owner controls the incentive mechanism and changes it unilaterally and frequently (resolution-tier rewards Jul 2026, per-tier Veo video pricing) \u2014 miners are exposed to mechanism risk. No third-party security audit found. Detection accuracy claims (88\u201395%, and the 19-benchmark paper) are self-published and not independently reproduced. One operational flag for anyone monitoring this subnet: the @BitMindAI handle has been dormant since 26 May 2026 \u2014 the live account is @bitmind. Monitoring the wrong handle would make this subnet look abandoned when it is not. CAVEATS: Could NOT verify revenue, a single named enterprise customer, or the alpha-buyback claim \u2014 treat all three as unproven. The existing record's $0 is defensible only as 'unproven', not as 'confirmed pre-revenue': they clearly sell a $100/mo tier, so some revenue almost certainly exists; I simply cannot size it. Their own marketing overstates in two places: bitmind.ai claims 'millions of users' and presence in '100+ countries' while their own May 2026 posts put Chrome extension users at 3,000 \u2014 those two claims cannot both be current and honest. The '95% accuracy' on the API page also sits against an 88% image-accuracy figure from their own subnet showcase; the number moves depending on the audience. Contributor concentration and closed-source product mean an investor is really underwriting one small company, not a decentralised network.",
    active_users: "A real paid product exists with published prices \u2014 https://bitmind.ai/product/api : Free $0 (100 requests/mo), Pro $100/mo (10,000+ requests/mo), Custom/Enterprise. Volume is self-disclosed at 'millions of detection requests a month' (https://x.com/bitmind/status/2085353950413304175, 6 Aug 2026). No revenue figure has ever been published, and crucially the free-vs-paid split is not disclosed \u2014 the bulk of that volume plausibly comes from the free web detector and free Chrome extension, so multiplying volume by the API price would fabricate a number. Claims of 'licensing and usage-based deals with enterprise customers' and alpha buybacks appear only in third-party podcast summaries with no figure and no named customer, which does not meet the bar for confirmed or estimated.",
    annual_revenue_usd: 0,
    revenue_confidence: "unknown",
    revenue_evidence: "A real paid product exists with published prices \u2014 https://bitmind.ai/product/api : Free $0 (100 requests/mo), Pro $100/mo (10,000+ requests/mo), Custom/Enterprise. Volume is self-disclosed at 'millions of detection requests a month' (https://x.com/bitmind/status/2085353950413304175, 6 Aug 2026). No revenue figure has ever been published, and crucially the free-vs-paid split is not disclosed \u2014 the bulk of that volume plausibly comes from the free web detector and free Chrome extension, so multiplying volume by the API price would fabricate a number. Claims of 'licensing and usage-based deals with enterprise customers' and alpha buybacks appear only in third-party podcast summaries with no figure and no named customer, which does not meet the bar for confirmed or estimated.",
    last_updated: "2026-08-12",
    sources: ["https://bitmind.ai", "https://bitmind.ai/product/api", "https://github.com/BitMind-AI/bitmind-subnet", "https://api.github.com/repos/BitMind-AI/bitmind-subnet/commits", "https://docs.bitmind.ai/architecture-summary", "https://x.com/bitmind/status/2085353950413304175", "https://x.com/bitmind/status/2087210049739661433", "https://subnetalpha.ai/subnet/bitmind/", "https://github.com/BitMind-AI", "https://discord.gg/kKQR98CrUn"],
