    benchmark_summary: "This netuid is dead. The on-chain subnet identity for netuid 39 has been overwritten to literally read subnet_name \"deprecated\", github_repo \"https://github.com/deprecated/deprecated\", contact \"deprecated@gmail.com\", description \"deprecated\" \u2014 i.e. the owner deliberately tombstoned it. Taostats reports emission 0, only 1 miner with incentive, and netuid 39 returns no row at all from the dTAO pool endpoint. The cause is Covenant AI's exit from Bittensor on 2026-04-09/10, when founder Sam Dare withdrew all three Covenant subnets \u2014 Templar (SN3), Basilica (SN39) and Grail (SN81) \u2014 calling Bittensor governance \"decentralization theatre\"; TAO fell ~20-27% on the news. The Basilica *product* still exists but off Bittensor: basilica.ai is a live GPU cloud (CLI + Python SDK `basilica-sdk` v0.33.0, `basilica up --gpu h100`, vLLM/SGLang deploys, credits topped up with TAO), and the repo was still being committed to on 2026-08-01. That product's value does not accrue to netuid 39 alpha holders. Anyone holding or scoring SN39 as \"Basilica the GPU marketplace\" is holding a tombstoned slot. AUDIT: The former codebase (https://github.com/one-covenant/basilica, MIT, 44 stars, ~1,500 commits from itzlambda/epappas) is real engineering, but it now serves an off-chain product. Governance risk is the headline item: the subnet owner unilaterally abandoned the netuid and publicly dumped ~37,000 TAO (~$10M) on exit. The successor product is materially centralised \u2014 api.basilica.ai/health returns {\"healthy_validators\":1,\"total_validators\":1}, a single validator single point of failure, plus centralised login/credit custody. No third-party security audit found for either the subnet or the product. CAVEATS: I could not determine whether anyone has re-registered or repurposed netuid 39 since the tombstone, or whether the slot will be recycled \u2014 treat the name field as \"deprecated\" until on-chain identity changes. I could not quantify basilica.ai's GPU-rental revenue: no public pricing page (basilica.ai/pricing is a 404), no disclosed ARR, and pricing is only visible after `basilica login`. Even if that revenue exists it belongs to Covenant AI, not to SN39. The AlphaGap record naming netuid 39 \"Basilica\" is stale by roughly four months and should be corrected.",
    active_users: "Netuid 39 has no product and no emissions: the on-chain identity is set to \"deprecated\" (https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/identity/v1, netuid 39) and the subnet reports emission 0 with no dTAO pool row (https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/latest/v1?netuid=39). Zero revenue is attributable to this netuid.",
