    subnet_id: 46,
    subnet_name: "Instant",
    benchmark_score: 32,
    benchmark_category: "AI Inference",
    vs_provider: "Groq, Together AI, Fireworks AI; on-network rivals Chutes (SN64), Targon (SN4), Lium (SN51)",
    cost_saving_pct: 0,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Instant is a brand-new occupant of netuid 46 building a decentralised marketplace for low-latency LLM inference \u2014 an OpenAI-compatible streaming API served by a miner network scored on latency, throughput and reliability. It positions itself explicitly as a specialised 'neocloud' for fast inference (their analogy: Groq) against the general-purpose compute subnets Chutes, Targon and Lium. As of 12 August 2026 essentially NOTHING is live: the public repo contains documentation only and states verbatim that the project 'is under active development and is not yet a production service' and that 'Public API access and operator onboarding are not open yet'. The website is a waitlist. The team announced the project in the first week of August 2026, began distributing API keys to testers on ~10 August, and said the first Instant mechanism launches the week of 17 August. Everything is roadmap. AUDIT: Effectively CLOSED SOURCE today. The public repo (created 29 July 2026) has 5 commits, 1 contributor (0pendansor), no license file, and its main branch was deliberately made 'a public documentation branch' \u2014 the only content is README, CONTRIBUTING, SECURITY and docs. All actual miner/validator code sits on a private/dev branch, so nothing about the scoring mechanism can be independently verified. No third-party audit. Single-person engineering bus factor. Validator set, key custody and emission distribution are entirely undisclosed. Note for buyers: netuid 46 previously hosted a different project; 'Instant' is a repurposing of the slot, so historical SN46 data, holders and any legacy reputation attach to a different team. Positive signals only: the owner key committed a 120K perpetual alpha lock (self-reported), and the team stated there is 'no other product or entity to benefit from Subnet 46 \u2014 all value is driven back to the subnet'. Named people: Dan/@opendansor (engineering) and @sebyrubino (growth, previously marketing at Compound and Maple Finance). CAVEATS: This is a pre-product, pre-code, pre-API subnet whose entire visible output is announcements. I could not verify the 120K alpha lock on-chain, could not see a single line of the mechanism code, could not find any benchmark result, and could not confirm the team has ever operated inference infrastructure at scale. The Groq comparison is aspiration, not measurement. The existing benchmark_score of 55 is far too generous for something with zero shippable surface \u2014 I have cut it to 32, and it belongs there until an API actually serves external traffic. It is NOT dead or parked (daily commits, active comms, funded owner key), so is_active is true. Risk of a rapid narrative-driven re-rate in either direction is high.",
    active_users: "The project's own README states 'Public API access and operator onboarding are not open yet' (https://github.com/instant-subnet/instant-subnet). instantsubnet.com is a waitlist signup with no pricing. The team posted on 12 Aug 2026 that 'the team continues internal testing' and the first mechanism launches the following week. Not present on the SubnetRadar/TAO Institute revenue tracker (https://subnetradar.com/alpha/revenue). There is no product to buy, therefore revenue is zero.",
