    benchmark_summary: "EvolAI is an LLM model-evaluation and small-model training subnet. Miners publish public HuggingFace models whose names must contain \"evolai\" on one of two tracks (transformer or mamba2, e.g. 0.4B-class models) and register them via an evolcli CLI; the validator loads the weights each round and scores them 60% on Quality (KL divergence from a Qwen3.5-9B reference, gated by how much <think> tokens help), 30% on Flow (Sharpe ratio of the KL improvement trend) and 10% on Side Quests (two short arithmetic tasks per round). This is a research/training mechanism with no end-user product, no API and no customer surface \u2014 nothing is sold and nothing is consumable by a buyer. Critically, the subnet is currently in owner-declared limbo: the on-chain subnet_name is literally \"wait (reproduce paper)\" and the description is \"redesign incentive\", i.e. the operator has publicly paused to reproduce a paper and rework the incentive. Chain state corroborates dormancy \u2014 emission 0, 1 active miner out of 114 registered keys, and 333 blocks since the last epoch step. The repo has not been pushed since 2026-06-27. The existing AlphaGap record (score 38, $0 revenue, researched 2026-07-21) overstates it; $0 revenue was correct but the subnet has since gone dormant. AUDIT: Open source under MIT, but the development posture is weak and anonymous. Every commit in the repository is authored by the generic identity \"default\" \u2014 a single unnamed author \u2014 and the GitHub contributors endpoint returns empty, so there is no verifiable team. The openevolai account hosts exactly one repository, created 2026-04-18, last pushed 2026-06-27. Repo is tiny (~307 KB), 1 star, 1 fork, no releases. The README's clone URL points at github.com/evolai-subnet/evolai while the on-chain field points at github.com/openevolai/evolai \u2014 an inconsistency suggesting an org rename or an abandoned second home. There is no third-party audit, no security policy, no disclosed validator set and no governance documentation. Owner coldkey 5GBmFsPkMDGcEcKwL69rCcbSko2xX2WTUzs6riW7d8XVqTpv. With 11 validators registered but zero emission and a stalled epoch cadence, the incentive mechanism is not currently doing observable work; the single anonymous operator is the sole point of failure and has unilaterally paused the network. CAVEATS: I could not identify the team, any funding, or any institutional backing. I could not determine how long the \"wait (reproduce paper)\" pause is intended to last or which paper is being reproduced \u2014 the operator gave no timeline anywhere I could find, and there is no website, X account or Discord to ask. I therefore cannot distinguish a genuine, temporary research pause from a slow abandonment, and I have scored it on observed state (dormant) rather than intent. Note this is a benign, honest self-label \u2014 the owner is not pretending to be live \u2014 but for an allocator the practical result is the same: a subnet producing nothing today. I also could not verify whether any miner models were ever successfully trained and scored, since there is no public leaderboard.",
    active_users: "There is no commercial surface at all: no website (on-chain subnet_url is empty), no pricing, no API product, no customers. The repo https://github.com/openevolai/evolai is purely miner/validator tooling (evolcli, requirements-validator.txt) with a README that only documents how to register a HuggingFace model for scoring. Chain state shows emission 0 and 1 active miner (https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/latest/v1?netuid=47), and the owner has renamed the subnet on chain to \"wait (reproduce paper)\" with description \"redesign incentive\".",
