    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. INACTIVE \u2014 parked, deregistered or abandoned.",
    benchmark_summary: "Dojo is Tensorplex Labs' subnet, originally a human-in-the-loop data-annotation and RLHF network where crowd workers scored model outputs, later relaunched as 'Dojo v2', a decentralised zero-sum GAN in which miners act as both generators and discriminators, competing to produce outputs judged superior to a high-quality baseline. Miners were meant to participate with no server, just a browser wallet, via the hosted app at dojo.network. As of 2026-08-12 essentially none of that is live. dojo.network now 301-redirects to the GitHub repo, so the product front door \u2014 the thing miners were told to use \u2014 no longer exists; testnet.dojo.network does not resolve at all. The tensorplex-labs/dojo repo has had no commits since 2025-11-03, the supporting repos (dojo-ui, dojo-worker-api, dojo-synthetic-gen, kami) all stopped in September 2025, and a dojo-archived repo sits alongside them. The final functional commits are telling: 'chore: disable sending task' and 'fix: skip score step count, and weight set on 100 percent burn'. Tensorplex Labs itself is still a going concern but has visibly redirected to Backprop Finance and to model releases (Sumo-T9-7B, DOJO-INTERFACE-CODER-7B). Treat SN52 as a wound-down subnet whose parent moved on. AUDIT: No third-party audit. Code is public under github.com/tensorplex-labs but the Dojo v2 repo carries no LICENSE file, has 0 stars, 5 contributors and is 9 months stale; the older dojo-archived repo (13 stars) is explicitly archived. Tensorplex Labs is a real, identifiable company (it also operates a validator service and publishes models on Hugging Face), which is a point in its favour relative to the anonymous teams elsewhere in this batch \u2014 but that does not help SN52. The decisive centralisation failure has already occurred and should be read as realised risk, not hypothetical: mining depended entirely on a team-hosted browser app at dojo.network, and that single point of failure has now been switched off, leaving the subnet unusable by its intended participants. Ten validators remain registered against one active miner, so on-chain weight setting is nominal. On-chain owner coldkey 5Fv1ZvNPsEvUN6jfia6Mv3ZoefZ6KdoowGMjkPMX61QwRLXx, registered 2024-10-07. Note neuron_registration_cost is pinned at 999999999 (min_burn == max registration burn floor), consistent with a subnet configured to discourage new registration. CAVEATS: I could not find any formal announcement from Tensorplex deprecating SN52 \u2014 docs.tensorplex.ai still documents the Dojo v2 mechanism as though current, and the subnet-docs repo (updated May 2026) still recommends SN52 as a template for other subnets. So the conclusion 'abandoned' is inferred from converging hard evidence (zero emission, one active miner, dead product domains, nine months of no commits, 100%-burn commits) rather than from a statement by the team, and I am flagging that inference explicitly. It is possible Tensorplex intends a third relaunch. The docs are, in my view, actively misleading: they present a live-sounding product whose front end has been turned into a GitHub redirect. is_active is set false and the score set to 12 on that basis; if the team ships a relaunch this needs immediate re-rating.",
    active_users: "https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/latest/v1?netuid=52 \u2014 as of block 8830473 (2026-08-12) netuid 52 reports emission '0' AND projected_emission '0' with active_miners: 1 against 10 validators, i.e. the subnet is receiving zero emission and has effectively no miner participation. Corroborated by https://github.com/tensorplex-labs/dojo commit 'fix: skip score step count, and weight set on 100 percent burn' (2025-10-24) \u2014 the last real code change was to handle the 100% burn state \u2014 and by dojo.network returning 'HTTP/2 301 location: https://github.com/tensorplex-labs/dojo', i.e. the product site has been replaced by a redirect to source. No pricing page, no customer, no revenue has ever been disclosed for Dojo.",
