    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "MIID (Multimodal Inorganic Identities Dataset) generates adversarial synthetic identity data used to stress-test financial-crime systems \u2014 sanctions screening, KYC, AML and fraud detection. Validators issue challenges, miners run models to produce identity variations, and validators score outputs on linguistic accuracy, realism and relevance. The subnet is the data engine underneath Yanez Compliance Inc.'s commercial product line, which is sold to banks, fintechs, IDV vendors and law enforcement as a no-code platform (Financial Crime Vulnerability Scanner, Agentic Decisioning, Adversarial Identity Data, Proof of Human Uniqueness) with stated use cases of testing/tuning, model validation and vendor selection. Live today: name-variation generation (Phase 1, mainnet since May 2025) \u2014 that is the only attack family verifiably in production. Roadmap: biometric attack families, synthetic documents, digital-presence simulation and financial-transaction modelling staggered across 2026-2027. Buyer is a compliance or financial-crime team; the sale is enterprise, not self-serve \u2014 there is no pricing page and no public API. AUDIT: Open source at github.com/yanez-compliance/MIID-subnet, created Feb 2025, actively maintained \u2014 100 commits in the ~2 months to 12 Aug 2026. But contribution is entirely in-house and thin: 6 contributors total, and the recent 100 commits come from just 4 accounts (Omar-A-Abaza, Omar-Yanez, asemYanezAI, asemothman), all Yanez staff. Unlike the anonymous SN7 team, leadership here is fully identified and credentialed \u2014 Jose Caldera (CEO), Bin Tang (CTO), Asem Othman (Chief AI Officer, 15+ yrs ML identity verification), Mark Quesenberry (Head of Sales) \u2014 and there is a real incorporated entity (Yanez Compliance Inc.). No third-party security or model audit found. Validators/miners are permissionless standard Bittensor roles. The dominant single point of failure is commercial, not cryptographic: the subnet exists to feed one company's enterprise sales motion, so if Yanez Compliance Inc. fails, SN54's demand side disappears entirely. CAVEATS: I could not verify a single named customer, any contract, or any revenue figure \u2014 the \"largest asset manager in the world\" client is an unnamed, unverifiable self-claim and I would not underwrite it. I also could not reach yanez.ai/blog or yanezcompliance.com/blog (both 404) to audit their full claim history, and my web-search budget ran out before I could chase founder podcast/X statements for a number. Overstated on their own materials: the marketing describes MIID as spanning \"deepfake-resistant biometrics\", synthetic documents and transaction modelling \u2014 per their own roadmap none of that is live; today it generates name variations. The Phase-4 \"opening to external institutions\" milestone was dated Sept 2025 and I found no confirmation it happened. Prior score of 67 looks slightly generous for a product whose live surface is one attack family and whose traction is entirely unevidenced; I have moved it to 58. Upside case if they ever disclose a contract value: this is one of the few subnets with a genuine enterprise buyer and a real sales hire.",
    active_users: "No figure could be established either way. Yanez asserts commercial traction \u2014 a blog claim that \"another public multibillion dollar organization\" (described as one of the largest asset managers in the world, validating its sanctions screening) became a client, and the macrocosmos guest post says Yanez \"is already delivering the adversarial data infrastructures that banks, IDV companies, and compliance vendors cannot build for themselves\" (https://macrocosmosai.substack.com/p/guest-post-bittensor-drives-unstoppable). But no client is named, no contract value, no ARR and no pricing page exists. The only hard number in their materials is capital, not revenue: $900K oversubscribed Seed Part A closed 22 Jul 2025 against a $600K target, from Deep Ventures with Yuma and BT Labs (https://www.yanezcompliance.com/post/yanez-closes-oversubscribed-seed-part-a-to-advance-bittensor-network-operations). Because they claim paying enterprise clients, this is explicitly NOT confirmed_pre_revenue \u2014 I simply cannot size it.",
    annual_revenue_usd: 0,
    revenue_confidence: "unknown",
    revenue_evidence: "No figure could be established either way. Yanez asserts commercial traction \u2014 a blog claim that \"another public multibillion dollar organization\" (described as one of the largest asset managers in the world, validating its sanctions screening) became a client, and the macrocosmos guest post says Yanez \"is already delivering the adversarial data infrastructures that banks, IDV companies, and compliance vendors cannot build for themselves\" (https://macrocosmosai.substack.com/p/guest-post-bittensor-drives-unstoppable). But no client is named, no contract value, no ARR and no pricing page exists. The only hard number in their materials is capital, not revenue: $900K oversubscribed Seed Part A closed 22 Jul 2025 against a $600K target, from Deep Ventures with Yuma and BT Labs (https://www.yanezcompliance.com/post/yanez-closes-oversubscribed-seed-part-a-to-advance-bittensor-network-operations). Because they claim paying enterprise clients, this is explicitly NOT confirmed_pre_revenue \u2014 I simply cannot size it.",
    last_updated: "2026-08-12",
