    benchmark_summary: "Ridges is an open-source competition platform for autonomous software-engineering agents. Miners submit an agent.py; validators pull the code, run it in sandboxes against hidden/randomised coding benchmarks (SWE-bench Verified, Polyglot, internal 'Harbor' tasks), and the highest-scoring agent takes emissions. That competition layer is genuinely live and usable today \u2014 there is a working CLI/Python toolkit (`ridges miner setup` / `run-local`), an inference gateway supporting OpenRouter/Targon/Chutes, docs at docs.ridges.ai, and a public leaderboard. The commercial layer, 'Ridgeline' (file a GitHub issue with a label, competing agents return a pull request), is NOT live: app.ridges.ai publishes tiers (Standard $9.99/mo for 10 credits; free for subnet stakers; x402 pay-per-use at $1.09/credit) but the Get Started button routes to /coming-soon, which states the dashboard and account experience are 'currently in development'. So: live subnet + published price list, no shipped paid product. Formerly named Agentao. AUDIT: Code is public at github.com/ridgesai/ridges and is real, heavy work \u2014 3,990 commits, 100 commits in the last 90 days, 21 contributors, 88 stars, last push 2026-08-11. NOT a template fork (own api/, execution/, inference_gateway/, validator/, k8s/ trees). Caveat: the repo has NO LICENSE file, so despite calling itself 'open source' the code is technically all-rights-reserved. Real centralisation points: Ridges operates the platform API and the inference gateway that every miner agent calls, plus a screener layer that gates submissions before validators see them \u2014 if Ridges' infrastructure goes down or censors, the competition stops. Validator keys are held by ordinary Bittensor validators, not by Ridges, but the evaluation harness they run is Ridges-authored and Ridges-hosted. No third-party security audit found. Discord: discord.gg/WeDvTnYDad; contact hello@ridges.ai (both from the on-chain identity record). CAVEATS: Blunt: the existing benchmark_score of 72 is too high for something with no purchasable product, and the existing $0 revenue is correct. The team's own stated goal was for product revenue to exceed emission cost by January 2026 \u2014 that has not happened; it is August 2026 and checkout is still 'coming soon'. Marketing claims I could not verify independently: '73-88% SWE-bench Verified and 96.3% Polyglot' and '5-7x cheaper than Claude Code and Codex' (from a promoter, @markjeffrey, March 2026, not from a neutral leaderboard); benchmark scores on hidden internal task sets are self-reported and not reproducible by an outsider. Note the launch price quoted in March 2026 was $29/mo for 100 PRs and the site now shows $9.99/mo for 10 credits \u2014 a ~3.5x increase in price per PR, which reads as pre-launch repricing rather than traction. Also a naming trap for anyone re-researching this: 'Ridgeline' also names an unrelated investment-management SaaS (ridgeline.ai, ~$104M ARR on getlatka) \u2014 that revenue figure has nothing to do with SN62. There is no X handle in the on-chain identity; @ridges_ai is the account used in practice.",
    active_users: "https://app.ridges.ai/coming-soon \u2014 'The Ridgeline dashboard and account experience are currently in development. Check back soon for access.' Pricing exists at https://app.ridges.ai/ ($9.99/mo / 10 credits; $1.09/credit via x402) but the checkout path is not open, so no customer can currently pay. Independent March 2026 review (https://ownyourmind.ai/tokenomics/bittensor-subnets-where-the-revenue-is/) states of SN62: 'No commercial product. No verified user metrics.' Funding is not revenue: ~$4M raised via OTC/token sales, incl. a disclosed $300k from DSV (https://dsvfund.com/otc-investment-ridges-ai/).",
