    benchmark_summary: "Decentralised VPN and residential-proxy infrastructure, run by Taofu Labs. The network has three node roles: Workers (simple machines that supply VPN bandwidth, no Bittensor neuron required), Miners (mining pools that aggregate workers, receive emissions, and distribute rewards to their workers as they see fit), and Validators (which score pools and act as the interface to end users). Emissions are scored linearly on worker-pool size, geographic uniqueness and a slowness penalty, with the scoring code public. What is live: the subnet itself since December 2024, a one-line worker install script, and programmatic access to residential WireGuard configs and socks5 proxies through a unified API. Taofu also ships Whalesurf, a consumer VPN app for Mac and Android built on TPN, described on their own site as free to try. Taofu Labs states it is backed by Delphi Ventures, Spacewhale Capital and G20, with no round sizes disclosed. AUDIT: The strongest decentralisation posture of the four. MIT-licensed, public since December 2024, 27 contributors, 11 stars, 10 forks, and 11 commits since May 2026 with the most recent push on 1 July 2026 \u2014 this is real sustained multi-party work, not a template fork. The mining-pool scoring code is published at a specific file path in the repo, so scoring logic is auditable rather than hidden behind a team API, which is materially better than SN37 or SN80. Risks: the worker install path instructs operators to curl a script from raw.githubusercontent and pipe it straight to bash, so a repo compromise would be a direct supply-chain compromise of every worker. Validators act as the user-facing interface, which concentrates trust for end users at the validator layer. Exit-node/VPN networks also carry inherent operator-trust risk \u2014 a malicious worker sees user traffic. No third-party security audit found. Taofu Labs is a named, VC-backed company, which reduces anonymity risk but means the roadmap depends on one company. CAVEATS: Revenue is deliberately marked unknown, not pre-revenue, and this is the judgement call a buyer should scrutinise. No pricing page exists on taofu.xyz or tpn.taofu.xyz, and the consumer apps are described as free to try \u2014 which points toward pre-revenue. But residential-proxy access is one of the most reliably monetised products in this category, Taofu is VC-backed and explicitly markets 'programmatic access' to developers, and I could NOT reach their API documentation (docs.tpn.taofu.xyz and api.tpn.taofu.xyz both failed DNS resolution from here) or whalesurf.app / whalesurf.com. So I could not check for a paid tier, rate limits or commercial terms \u2014 the single most likely place a price would be published. Do not read this as confirmed pre-revenue. The VC backing is asserted by Taofu Labs on their own site and I could not independently verify it with a funding announcement, and no round size is disclosed, so treat the Delphi Ventures claim as unconfirmed. The Discord link comes from a March 2026 metadata snapshot and I have not re-validated the invite. WebSearch budget was exhausted, blocking any sweep for founder revenue statements or funding coverage.",
