    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Harnyx (SN67) commoditises deep research: a user query is fanned out to a competitive swarm of miners, each building its own research pipeline \u2014 query planning, retrieval, ranking, cross-checking, synthesis \u2014 and every claim in the returned JSON report is tied to a reproducible citation so validators can verify factuality. Miners submit Python agents; validators run them sandboxed against research tasks with a stronger reference answer and set weights on-chain. Miners can now mix five search backends per task (Desearch, Parallel, Firecrawl, Exa, Tavily). A public benchmark dashboard exists at dashboard.harnyx.ai/benchmark and a BrowseComp suite was added on 12 August 2026. The subnet mechanism is LIVE and under heavy iteration. The commercial product is NOT: the customer-facing deep-research API is waitlist-only, with the site promising 'We'll email you once when API access is ready'. AUDIT: Source-available with a real, substantial codebase at https://github.com/harnyx/harnyx \u2014 full uv workspace with validator/, miner/, commons/, packages/miner-sdk, sandbox, pytest and coverage config, ~700 human commits across 1,294+ PRs. Clearly the heaviest engineering effort of these four, and not a template fork. BUT: there is NO LICENSE file in the repo, so it is source-available rather than legally open source \u2014 a real consideration for anyone forking or running a validator. Validator releases are pushed by an automated bot (harnyx-validator-version-bump-bot) bumping a 'repo-owned validator version' several times a day, which means the subnet owner effectively controls what code every validator runs \u2014 a genuine single point of control and the main decentralisation risk here. Human bus factor is 2 (0kmark ~389 commits, shrimp-acrylic ~64). Harnyx has no dedicated Discord server; its listed 'discord' is a channel inside the main Bittensor server. Contact is via brightmount.co. The site claims backing from Digital Currency Group, Ethos Fund and Bluepoint. Positive governance signal: the team publicly welcomed the independent RT21/21RoundTable validator, stating more independent validators is the goal. No third-party security audit found. CAVEATS: The 'Backed by DCG / Ethos Fund / Bluepoint' claim is asserted on their own homepage and I could NOT independently corroborate it \u2014 no funding announcement, press release, round size or date surfaced in search. Treat it as unverified until a primary source appears. The '10x lower cost per query' and the DRACO/DeepSearchQA parity claims are self-published; Harnyx explicitly does not publish its own proprietary benchmark results against those standards, so the headline comparison is against competitor list prices, not a measured head-to-head. No paying customer, no public pricing, no API access \u2014 so despite excellent engineering there is zero evidence of demand. Existing recorded revenue of $0 is correct. Existing benchmark_score of 55 is about right; I have set 58 to reflect the code quality and validator-diversity posture, but it cannot go higher while the product is behind a waitlist.",
    active_users: "https://harnyx.ai/ \u2014 the API is not public; the site runs a waitlist with 'We'll email you once when API access is ready' and publishes no Harnyx price, only competitor per-query costs (OpenAI $1.83, Gemini $3.68, Perplexity $1.54) against a $0.15-$0.37/query target. No customers named. Absent from the SubnetRadar/TAO Institute external-revenue tracker (https://subnetradar.com/alpha/revenue). A 12 Aug 2026 team post describes reshaping tasks around 'the questions a deep-research API gets' \u2014 i.e. they are still designing toward the product, not billing for it.",
