    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "NOVA is a decentralised virtual drug-screening network run by Metanova Labs, a crypto-native biotech. Miners generate candidate small molecules from the SAVI-2020 combinatorial chemical space (~1.75B synthesizable molecules, marketed as ~65B via combinatorial expansion) and validators score them with PSICHIC, a fixed deterministic binding-affinity oracle, in roughly hourly on-chain tournaments against a rotating protein target. What is verifiably live today is the competition machinery itself: three continuous ML competitions (small molecules, nanobodies, chemical search algorithms), a public dashboard, and a repo with 629 commits that was still being merged the morning of 2026-08-12. What is NOT live is everything that would make it a business: wet-lab validation of hits, CRO partnerships, licensing of candidate compounds, and 'screening as a service' are all described as forthcoming. There is no buyer today \u2014 miners are paid in subnet alpha, and no pharma or biotech customer has been named. AUDIT: Code is public at github.com/metanova-labs/nova but there is NO LICENSE file in the repo \u2014 publicly readable is not the same as open source, and downstream reuse rights are legally unclear. Contributor base is effectively two people (cosmic-amanita 414 commits, urdof7 202; a third contributor has 2), so it is a single-team project with heavy key-person risk. The repo is generated from cosmic-amanita/subnet-template, but the domain logic (combinatorial_db, external_tools, neurons) is genuine original work, not a template fork. Scoring is centralised by design: PSICHIC is a single fixed third-party model acting as the sole oracle \u2014 reproducible and bias-free, but a single point of failure and a single gameable surface if the model is ever inverted. Challenge/target selection is set by the subnet owner. Validators require dual GPUs, which structurally limits the validator set. The project's linked 'Discord' is the generic Bittensor server, not its own community server. No third-party security or scientific audit found. CAVEATS: I could not verify any wet-lab result, CRO agreement, university partnership or pharma collaboration \u2014 all are asserted as roadmap and none is named. I could not find any funding round, investor, or balance-sheet information for Metanova Labs. The '65 billion molecules' figure is a combinatorial expansion of a ~1.75B synthesizable library, not 65B enumerated compounds, and is overstated in their marketing. The claim that this 'could halve early-stage drug discovery costs' is unsupported by any published benchmark. The existing AlphaGap score of 72 is too generous for a project with zero revenue, zero named customers and zero validated hits; I have marked it down to 62. Prior recorded revenue of $0 was correct and remains correct.",
