    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. INACTIVE \u2014 parked, deregistered or abandoned.",
    benchmark_summary: "DO NOT CARRY THE 'NexisGen' NAME OR THE SCORE OF 58 FORWARD \u2014 this slot has been recycled. On-chain data at block 8830463 (2026-08-12T19:18:24Z) shows netuid 70 has registration_timestamp 2026-08-12T03:00:00Z at block 8825571, with a fresh 511.5 TAO subnet registration lock paid by owner 5EP42hSodDgwNnXx1BrNwkJZ4ScMf22SJSqNqAq3SyjZib5E. The slot was therefore roughly 16 hours old when researched. For contrast, netuids 27, 77 and 112 carry their original registration dates of 2023-11-16, 2025-03-14 and 2025-05-25. The new occupant has set NO on-chain identity (subnet_name resolves to 'Unknown', with null github, url, discord and description) and has 5 active keys, 0 validators and 0 miners \u2014 a completely empty network. Separately, the NexisGen project (a 'commissions house' for commissioned AI training datasets, spec VIDEO_V1 video clips with grounded captions and chain-of-custody provenance) still has a live marketing site at nexisgen.ai, but it is visibly failing: its own live counters read 0 miners, 0 certified records and 0 validators in quorum, its homepage prints 'Live counters: Bad Gateway', its /docs page cannot load its own OpenAPI spec, and its validation API returns HTTP 502 on both /healthz and /v1/get_latest_total_score. There is no purchasable product \u2014 the 'commission' page is a lead-capture brief form that states 'A commission is not a checkout'. AUDIT: For the current occupant there is nothing to assess: no identity, no repo, no site, no validators, no miners. Treat it as an unallocated slot until an identity is set. For the departed NexisGen deployment: the code at github.com/RendixNetwork/nexisgen is public but has NO license file, last push 2026-07-17, and 42 of 43 commits from a single developer (xeon0359) \u2014 severe key-man risk. Architecture was heavily centralised on operator-run infrastructure: three Cloudflare R2 buckets (nexis-miner, nexis-record-info, nexis-owner-db) plus an 'owner-validator' role that certified datasets, and a single hosted validation API at api.nexisgen.ai \u2014 which is currently returning 502, meaning the operator's single point of failure has in fact failed. No third-party audit found. Recent commit history ('remove total_score.json completely', 'set weight based on individual validator score directly') shows they were actively trying to reduce reliance on that central score file, but the work stopped in July. CAVEATS: The single most important caveat: I am inferring from chain data that netuid 70 was deregistered and recycled, because the subnet registration timestamp is today and the owner key is new. I could NOT independently confirm via an announcement that NexisGen was the prior occupant or why it dropped, and I could not reach the team (no X API key available in this environment to check @nexisgen_ai, and their Discord was not joined). It is also possible \u2014 though the evidence weighs against it \u2014 that NexisGen itself deregistered and immediately re-registered the same slot under a new key; even in that case the slot is a blank, zero-neuron network today and must not be scored on the old profile. Note that taostats' identity endpoint still returns a stale cached AI-written 'summary' describing Nexisgen for netuid 70 even though subnet_name is 'Unknown' and every link field is null \u2014 do not mistake that cached summary for a live on-chain identity, it is exactly the trap that would perpetuate the wrong name. Also do not confuse nexisgen.com (an unrelated IT agency, 'Nexisgen Technology') with nexisgen.ai. Overstated on their materials: nexisgen.ai presents a nine-station 'commissions house' with a decentralized producer network and validator quorum, while its own dashboard reports zero miners, zero validators and zero certified records. This entry needs a re-check in a few weeks once whoever bought the slot publishes an identity.",
    active_users: "The current netuid 70 is a ~16-hour-old empty registration with zero validators, zero miners and no published product, so it cannot have revenue: https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/latest/v1 returns for netuid 70 registration_timestamp '2026-08-12T03:00:00Z', active_validators 0, active_miners 0, active_keys 5, emission '0'. The prior NexisGen occupant also never showed revenue: no pricing appears anywhere on https://www.nexisgen.ai/commission, which explicitly says 'A commission is not a checkout' and collects a brief by email instead, and its pipeline status is 'LOT 001 In production / LOT 002+ Reserved' with all network counters at zero.",
