    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Leadpoet sells B2B intent-driven sales leads. Miners on SN71 run AI agents that scrape and score public buying signals (job postings, tech-stack changes, funding rounds, competitor engagement, community forums) and validators score submitted leads for ICP fit and accuracy. Two live tracks: a Research Lab where miners run auto-research loops to improve the shared sales agent, and Fulfillment where miners compete on real inbound lead requests. What is verifiably live today: the open-source subnet code, a public live dashboard at subnet71.com tracking lead inventory, a commercial funnel at leadpoet.com, and a disclosed customer base. Buying is sales-led (Cal.com intro call) \u2014 there is no self-serve pricing page, so ACV and unit economics are not publicly inspectable. Payment is described as running through a token-burning mechanism on the alpha token, with fiat also accepted. AUDIT: Code is open source under MIT at github.com/leadpoet/leadpoet and the repo is genuinely active \u2014 3,355 commits, 29 contributors, 101-313 commits per week over the last two months (checked 12 Aug 2026). Caveat on that contributor count: several top contributors (ifrit98, unconst, steffencruz, shibshib, Eugene-hu) are Opentensor Foundation identities inherited from the Bittensor subnet template, so effective in-house engineering is concentrated in one person (Pranav-create, 2,315 of 3,355 commits) plus the CEO (gzaentz, 145). That is a severe key-person risk. Architecturally, both Research Lab and Fulfillment outputs pass through a gateway TEE whose enclave-held signing key signs receipts, scoring bundles and allocation records \u2014 that gateway is operated by the subnet owner and is a hard single point of failure and a centralisation point: if it stops signing, scoring stops. Recent commits reference Supabase reads bound to identity encoding, i.e. a centralised hosted database in the critical path. No third-party security or code audit found. No independent audit of the revenue figure either \u2014 Forbes and Astrid both trace back to company statements. Note the conflict of interest on the Astrid RNS: Astrid is both an investor in and a token holder of SN71, so it is not a disinterested verifier. CAVEATS: The $1M ARR / 26 customers figure is dated Q1 2026 (Forbes, 2 Feb 2026; restated by Astrid, 20 Mar 2026). It is now mid-August 2026 and I found NO updated revenue disclosure \u2014 the number could be materially higher or lower today, and it should be treated as a ~6-month-old point estimate, not current ARR. It is self-reported and not audited; no customer is named publicly. The pre-seed was only $750k against a claimed $1M ARR, which is an unusually high revenue-to-funding ratio for a 4-5 person company and warrants scepticism about revenue quality (one-off lead-pack purchases can be counted as \"annualized\"). \"Annualized run rate\" from a single quarter is the weakest form of revenue claim. A seed round was signalled as \"coming\" \u2014 I found no evidence it closed. Marketing claims I could not verify: the \"25,000+ high-quality leads per day\" throughput figure, the 88-94% confidence scores shown on the site (explicitly illustrative), and \"12+ sources\". No pricing page means I could not sanity-check ARR against price \u00d7 customers.",
    active_users: "https://www.forbes.com/sites/charliefink/2026/02/02/ai-driven-intent-data-gains-traction-as-sales-teams-look-beyond-lead-lists/ \u2014 Forbes (2 Feb 2026) reports Leadpoet \"reached a one million dollar annualized run rate across 26 B2B customers\" in its first quarter after launch, alongside a $750,000 pre-seed from DSV Fund and Astrid. Independently repeated in a regulated AQSE company announcement by Astrid Intelligence plc: https://www.investegate.co.uk/announcement/rns/astrid-intelligence-plc--astr/expansion-of-position-in-subnet-71-leadpoet-/9483519 (20 Mar 2026), which also discloses Astrid holding ~2,366 TAO-equivalent SN71 tokens worth ~\u00a3500,000.",
    annual_revenue_usd: 1000000,
    revenue_confidence: "confirmed",
    revenue_evidence: "https://www.forbes.com/sites/charliefink/2026/02/02/ai-driven-intent-data-gains-traction-as-sales-teams-look-beyond-lead-lists/ \u2014 Forbes (2 Feb 2026) reports Leadpoet \"reached a one million dollar annualized run rate across 26 B2B customers\" in its first quarter after launch, alongside a $750,000 pre-seed from DSV Fund and Astrid. Independently repeated in a regulated AQSE company announcement by Astrid Intelligence plc: https://www.investegate.co.uk/announcement/rns/astrid-intelligence-plc--astr/expansion-of-position-in-subnet-71-leadpoet-/9483519 (20 Mar 2026), which also discloses Astrid holding ~2,366 TAO-equivalent SN71 tokens worth ~\u00a3500,000.",
    last_updated: "2026-08-12",
    sources: ["https://www.forbes.com/sites/charliefink/2026/02/02/ai-driven-intent-data-gains-traction-as-sales-teams-look-beyond-lead-lists/", "https://www.investegate.co.uk/announcement/rns/astrid-intelligence-plc--astr/expansion-of-position-in-subnet-71-leadpoet-/9483519", "https://github.com/leadpoet/leadpoet", "https://api.github.com/repos/leadpoet/leadpoet/contributors", "https://leadpoet.com", "https://subnet71.com/", "https://subnetalpha.ai/subnet/leadpoet/", "https://uk.finance.yahoo.com/news/astrid-intelligence-expands-stake-bittensor-072900367.html", "https://www.tao.app/subnets/71", "https://discord.gg/tMcmbPKvz"],
