    cost_saving_pct: 0,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. INACTIVE \u2014 parked, deregistered or abandoned.",
    benchmark_summary: "StreetVision was NATIX Network's Bittensor subnet: miners ran image-classification and object-detection models (roadwork detection, then wider street-scene tasks) over 360-degree multi-camera footage collected by NATIX's DePIN fleet (VX360 Tesla dongles and the Drive& phone app), with challenges dealt out by a NATIX-run central API. As of 2026-08-12 the subnet is deliberately halted and has been for three months. The reference validator on main HEAD returns immediately from forward() ('Subnet halted: skipping challenge forward pass') and hard-codes set_weights to uids=[0], weights=[65535], burning 100% of miner emissions to UID 0; a companion commit documented setting owner_cut to 0 and raising min_burn to deter registrations. Chain data confirms it: emission 0, weights_version 0, difficulty pinned at max, and exactly 1 active miner against 7 validators. NATIX said on 2026-05-07 the pause was intentional and the subnet would be 'back online in 6-8 weeks'; that window expired around early July and there has been no code commit since 2026-05-07 and no restart. The parent company is alive and shipping (190K+ hours of monthly footage, Orbis world models, open datasets on HuggingFace) but none of that currently runs through subnet 72. AUDIT: MIT licensed, 11 contributors, real (non-template) code \u2014 but heavily centralised even before the halt: validators pull every challenge and report every result to a NATIX-operated API (natix/validator/api_client.py: fetch_api_challenge, statistics_assign_task, statistics_report_task_batch), so NATIX controlled task flow and scoring inputs. The halt itself was executed unilaterally by the owner via reference-validator code plus btcli sudo params (owner_cut, min_burn), which demonstrates the owner can switch the subnet's economics off at will \u2014 a single point of failure holders should price in. Data supply is 100% dependent on NATIX's proprietary fleet; there is no permissionless data source. No third-party security audit found. CAVEATS: I could not verify whether any restart is scheduled \u2014 NATIX's public channels have not mentioned the subnet's return since the 2026-05-07 'back in 6-8 weeks' thread, and its August progress update covers company milestones with no subnet 72 restart. I did not independently confirm that every running validator uses the halted reference code (a validator could run older code), but with on-chain emission at 0 and 1 active miner the practical outcome is the same. NATIX's own marketing (2.89M drivers, partners including Google/NVIDIA/Amazon) describes the company, NOT the subnet \u2014 treating those partner logos as subnet traction would be a serious overstatement. The prior benchmark of 58 was recorded 2026-07-21, after the halt, and looks stale/wrong.",
    active_users: "Subnet-level revenue is structurally zero while halted: https://github.com/natixnetwork/streetvision-subnet/commit (chore: burn rewards) adds docs/subnet-halt.md \u2014 'All miner rewards are burned by directing 100% of validator weights to UID 0' and instructs 'btcli sudo set --param owner_cut --value 0 --netuid 72'. Chain confirms emission '0' (taostats /api/subnet/latest/v1?netuid=72, block 8830427, 2026-08-12). NATIX the company sells a $379 VX360 device (https://www.natix.network) and a data marketplace, but discloses no revenue figure and none of it is attributable to the subnet.",
    annual_revenue_usd: 0,
    revenue_confidence: "confirmed_pre_revenue",
    revenue_evidence: "Subnet-level revenue is structurally zero while halted: https://github.com/natixnetwork/streetvision-subnet/commit (chore: burn rewards) adds docs/subnet-halt.md \u2014 'All miner rewards are burned by directing 100% of validator weights to UID 0' and instructs 'btcli sudo set --param owner_cut --value 0 --netuid 72'. Chain confirms emission '0' (taostats /api/subnet/latest/v1?netuid=72, block 8830427, 2026-08-12). NATIX the company sells a $379 VX360 device (https://www.natix.network) and a data marketplace, but discloses no revenue figure and none of it is attributable to the subnet.",
    last_updated: "2026-08-12",
    sources: ["https://github.com/natixnetwork/streetvision-subnet", "https://github.com/natixnetwork/streetvision-subnet/commits/main", "https://github.com/natixnetwork/streetvision-subnet/blob/main/natix/validator/forward.py", "https://github.com/natixnetwork/streetvision-subnet/blob/main/natix/base/validator.py", "https://www.natix.network/", "https://x.com/NATIXNetwork", "https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/latest/v1?netuid=72", "https://api.taostats.io/api/dtao/pool/latest/v1?netuid=72", "https://discord.gg/natixnetwork"],
