    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "A brand-new subnet for improving vision-language-action (VLA) models for robotics. Miners fine-tune the pi-0.5 base model, upload complete checkpoints to Hugging Face, pay an evaluation burn, and announce the model commit on chain; a scoring service evaluates submissions across six LIBERO task suites in MuJoCo and a leaderboard ranks them. What is live: two public MIT-licensed repos \u2014 openroboto-subnet (miner, protocol helpers, weight-setting validator, training runner) and openroboto-evaluation (the parallel reproducible LIBERO scoring harness) \u2014 both actively pushed as of 8 August 2026, plus documented seed-derivation using future block hashes and drand for tamper-resistance. There is no buyer-facing product, no API to purchase, and no pricing. The output is an open leaderboard of robotics model checkpoints, not a sellable service. This netuid previously hosted 'dogelayer', a Scrypt merged-mining pool project; OpenRoboto is a new occupant, not a rename. AUDIT: Miner code, protocol/chain commitment formats, weight-setting logic, evaluation rules, LIBERO tooling and seed derivation are all public under MIT. The team is explicit about the trust boundary, which is a point in its favour, but that boundary is wide: held-out task data, the scoring service deployment, and subnet-owner operational tools are all closed and team-run. Miners read a team-published control.json and a team-run read-only API. That means the subnet owner unilaterally decides scores \u2014 a clear single point of failure. Seed derivation is genuinely non-gameable (future block hash plus drand, neither of which exists at submission time). Zero external contributors, zero stars, zero forks on both repos; all 9 recent commits are from the founding team. No third-party audit. I could not identify the team members by name from any primary source. CAVEATS: This subnet was NEVER BENCHMARKED and there is very little external signal to work with. openroboto.ai is a JavaScript-rendered single-page app that returned only its title heading to my fetcher, so I could not read its leaderboard, team or funding sections \u2014 my entire read of this project comes from its GitHub repos and their READMEs. I therefore cannot confirm whether any miners besides the founders are actually competing, which is the key question for whether this subnet is real. The engineering quality of the code and documentation is genuinely above average for a new subnet, but it is three weeks old with no external traction, so the score reflects promise, not proof. WebSearch budget was exhausted, so I could not check X or funding databases for the team's backing. Anyone relying on this should re-check the leaderboard directly in a browser before allocating.",
    active_users: "https://github.com/openroboto-ai/openroboto-subnet \u2014 the README documents a one-way value flow only: miners pay an evaluation burn in alpha to have checkpoints scored. There is no customer-facing product, no pricing page, and no paid API on openroboto.ai. The subnet's repos were created 22 and 29 July 2026, roughly three weeks before this assessment, so revenue at this stage is not plausible.",
    annual_revenue_usd: 0,
    revenue_confidence: "confirmed_pre_revenue",
    revenue_evidence: "https://github.com/openroboto-ai/openroboto-subnet \u2014 the README documents a one-way value flow only: miners pay an evaluation burn in alpha to have checkpoints scored. There is no customer-facing product, no pricing page, and no paid API on openroboto.ai. The subnet's repos were created 22 and 29 July 2026, roughly three weeks before this assessment, so revenue at this stage is not plausible.",
