    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. INACTIVE \u2014 parked, deregistered or abandoned.",
    benchmark_summary: "Grail was Covenant AI's verifiable post-training subnet: a protocol for cryptographically provable LLM inference, coordinating miners, validators and trainers to generate and verify rollouts tied to a specific model and input, across GPU-kernel, maths and code-generation environments. It is now abandoned. Covenant AI (Templar SN3, Basilica SN39, Grail SN81) publicly quit the Bittensor ecosystem on 2026-04-09, calling the governance 'decentralization theatre'; TAO fell 15-27% on the news and Grail's alpha fell ~68%. The owner then wiped the subnet's on-chain identity to placeholder junk. Nothing is live, nothing is buyable, no successor team has claimed it. AUDIT: Was open source (github.com/one-covenant/grail, 25 stars) with public W&B and Grafana dashboards \u2014 but the repo has had zero commits since 2026-04-10 (final commit: 'chore: bump version to 0.0.60' by ErfanMhi), i.e. the day after the exit announcement. No third-party audit. The decisive governance fact: the owner coldkey 5DUELqJMeY6tA7652ooUUvU9TgUCi5hnv9o66nC8Zjw7BtW5 still holds the subnet and used that control to overwrite the on-chain identity with 'deprecated' across every field (name, description, contact 'deprecated@gmail.com', logo 'https://deprecated.png', discord 'deprecated') \u2014 the same treatment applied to Covenant's SN3. An owner who can unilaterally erase a subnet's identity, and did, while dumping ~37,000 TAO of alpha, is the single point of failure. Anyone buying SN81 alpha is buying an orphaned emission stream with no maintainer. CAVEATS: One genuine ambiguity a buyer must understand: the subnet is not chain-dead. As of 2026-08-12 it still shows 6 validators and 72 of 256 neurons with non-zero incentive, so weights are still being set and emission is still flowing to somebody. But ema_tao_flow is 0 and recycled_24_hours is 0 \u2014 no one is paying to register any more. My read is that residual validator/miner infrastructure is still turning on unmaintained code with no owner behind it; I could NOT confirm any successor team, fork or rescue effort, and I looked. Treat the 72 earning miners as a zombie process, not as product usage. This subnet was never previously benchmarked, so there is no prior figure to compare; I am scoring it 12 under the abandoned-subnet rule. Also note the supplied name 'Grail' is now stale on-chain \u2014 the registered subnet_name is literally the string 'deprecated', and tao.app titles the page 'SN81 - deprecated'.",
    active_users: "Never monetised. Grail was a research protocol with no pricing, no API product and no customers at any point; the only inflow was TAO emission. It is now abandoned, so no revenue exists or will. Evidenced by the wiped on-chain identity (subnet_url is empty string, github_repo 'https://github.com/deprecated/deprecated') at https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/identity/v1 and the dead repo at https://github.com/one-covenant/grail.",
