    cost_saving_pct: 80,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "CliqueAI (operated by the pseudonymous 'toptensor') runs a distributed competition to approximate the Maximum Clique Problem, an NP-hard graph problem. A validator draws a graph from an internal problem database, samples miners with difficulty-adjusted probability, and scores returned cliques on both optimality and algorithmic diversity, updating an EMA reputation. Three live difficulty tiers are documented (medium 290-300 vertices, hard 490-500, very hard 690-700) under 6-30 second time limits. The code is genuine and purpose-built rather than a template fork \u2014 about 182 KB across 64 files including a scattering-GNN clique model with a checkpoint, a graph codec, and custom scoring \u2014 and releases have shipped steadily (v0.0.11 in January through v0.0.17 on 2026-07-21). Participation is real: 237 active miners and 7 validators on chain, with ~0.96 TAO recycled in registrations in the last 24h. What does NOT exist is any commercial surface: cliqueai.toptensor.ai is a Three.js splash page with a miner scoreboard and nothing else, there is no API, no docs site, no pricing, no named users of the solver output, and no X account. AUDIT: Code is public on GitHub but there is NO license file, so it is not legally open source. Commits are squashed release drops from a single 'toptensor-deployer' bot account (1 contributor total), so there is no visible team, no named individuals and no way to assess who holds the owner coldkey (5DqEjRLyNN8k3WbEXhA36tyGG4YpWyPEcVSTa47XxspNHhc3) beyond an anonymous handle; toptensor.ai has MX records but serves no site. The validator draws problems from an operator-controlled database and logs to the team's W&B, so problem selection and the ground-truth 'best known' solutions are trusted inputs. No third-party audit exists. Additional live risk: on-chain subnet_emission_enabled is currently false (the spec-440 emission gate) with projected_emission ~0.019, so it is sitting below the demand bar. CAVEATS: I could not identify the team behind 'toptensor' at all \u2014 no X account, no LinkedIn, no about page, no Discord invite beyond a Bittensor-server channel ID. I could not verify that solving max-clique instances produces anything of downstream commercial value here; the project itself makes no such claim, so treat any framing of it as a drug-discovery/fraud-detection/portfolio product as unsupported. The 237 active miners are the strongest positive signal but they are chasing emissions, not customer demand, so this is not evidence of product traction. The existing benchmark of 52 (last researched 2026-04-07) overrates it given the absence of any commercial surface; I lowered it to 40.",
    active_users: "I checked the site, the repo and both docs files: there is no pricing page, no customer API, no product tier and no way to buy anything. https://cliqueai.toptensor.ai/ renders only the title, 'Maximum Clique Mechanism', 'Structured Problem Types' and 'Miner Scoreboard' (verified by extracting strings from the site's JS bundle /assets/index-BbdpaL7n.js). https://github.com/toptensor/CliqueAI documents miner/validator startup only. The subnet's solved cliques are not sold to anyone.",
    annual_revenue_usd: 0,
    revenue_confidence: "confirmed_pre_revenue",
    revenue_evidence: "I checked the site, the repo and both docs files: there is no pricing page, no customer API, no product tier and no way to buy anything. https://cliqueai.toptensor.ai/ renders only the title, 'Maximum Clique Mechanism', 'Structured Problem Types' and 'Miner Scoreboard' (verified by extracting strings from the site's JS bundle /assets/index-BbdpaL7n.js). https://github.com/toptensor/CliqueAI documents miner/validator startup only. The subnet's solved cliques are not sold to anyone.",
    last_updated: "2026-08-12",
    sources: ["https://github.com/toptensor/CliqueAI", "https://github.com/toptensor/CliqueAI/blob/main/docs/mechanism.md", "https://github.com/toptensor/CliqueAI/releases", "https://cliqueai.toptensor.ai/", "https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/latest/v1?netuid=83", "https://api.taostats.io/api/dtao/pool/latest/v1?netuid=83"],
