    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Investing88 runs a decentralised asset-management tournament: miners submit structured portfolio strategies as files, and validators score them daily on real market data using a published formula combining return, volatility, drawdown, slippage and timeframe over a 50-day rolling window. Phase I (TAO/alpha staking strategies) went live April 2025 and Phase II (US large-cap equities, with MOO/MOC rebalancing and real NYSE/NASDAQ cut-off times) in July 2025; UID space and emissions are split by an asset ratio, currently 50/50. Live and usable today: the strategy tournament, a public leaderboard at db.investing88.ai, a zero-code miner UI (kym.investing88.ai), a public API (api.investing88.ai), and a local backtester (simst). The commercial layer is the 88 Quant Fund, launched December 2025 as a partnership with TrustedStake, a TAO/alpha fund driven by the subnet's ensemble strategy. Phases III-IV (forex, commodities, global multi-asset) and the retail-facing AUM app on Interactive Brokers' institutional program remain roadmap. AUDIT: Effectively a single-developer project: the repo has exactly ONE contributor (mobiusfund, all 67 commits) and only 7 commits in the last 90 days \u2014 the thinnest development activity of these four. README claims MIT but there is NO LICENSE file, and the MIT text pasted into the README is unmodified Opentensor Foundation boilerplate (copyright \u00a9 2024 Opentensor Foundation), so the actual licensing of Mobius Fund's own code is unsettled. Serious centralisation surface: validators depend on owner-run endpoints (api.investing88.ai serves the tradable asset list and the asset ratio that partitions emissions), so the subnet owner unilaterally controls both the investable universe and the emission split between asset classes. The scoring formula is published, but the commercially valuable part \u2014 the 'meta/ensemble strategy' built from top miner outputs and used to run the fund \u2014 is proprietary and entirely off-chain, so miners contribute the alpha and cannot verify how it is combined or monetised. Miner entry requires 192 alpha staked plus 64 alpha paid per coldkey, an owner-set toll. Custody and execution for the 88 Quant Fund sit with TrustedStake, an additional off-chain counterparty. No third-party audit, no fund administrator, no auditor, and no regulatory registration found for the fund. CAVEATS: TRAP \u2014 do not misread the repo: the commit 'Initial fund 2000 Tao' (2026-08-05) and the README line 'we assume fund = 2000 Tao' are the SIMULATED starting capital constant used in the scoring backtest, raised from 1,000 to account for market growth. They are NOT assets under management. Anyone skimming the repo will read that as AUM and be wrong. Separately, the '$10M USD' figure for US stocks in the same formula is also a simulation constant, not capital. I could not verify the 1,400 TAO 88 Quant Fund AUM from a primary source, could not find any fee terms, could not confirm how many clients exist, and could not verify the claimed Interactive Brokers institutional-program relationship. The '$145 trillion asset management industry' TAM framing on the site is pure marketing. The existing benchmark of 68 is too high for a one-developer repo with no verified revenue and no published fee schedule; I set 55, with credit for the fact that a real fund with real (small) client capital does appear to exist, which is more than most subnets can say. Previous recorded revenue of $0 is not contradicted by anything I found.",
    active_users: "No fee schedule, management fee, performance fee or minimum investment is published anywhere I could reach \u2014 not on investing88.ai, not on stakingalpha.com (which 301-redirects to investing88.ai), not on trustedstake.ai, and not in the repo. The only quantity in circulation is a secondhand AUM figure of 'over 1,400 TAO' for the 88 Quant Fund with onboarding paused (via https://subnetalpha.ai/subnet/investing/); I could not reach a primary source for it. Sanity arithmetic on that figure at TAO $199.63 (CoinGecko, 2026-08-12): 1,400 TAO ~= $279,000 AUM; even at an aggressive 2-and-20 with a 20% gross year that is roughly $5,600 management fee + ~$11,000 performance fee, i.e. under ~$17k/yr \u2014 immaterial either way. Their own overview doc (Investing/doc/Subnet88.md) still says 'we will start acquiring clients when the clear alpha edge emerges' and that the frontend AUM app is 'in the alpha development stage', which reads pre-revenue. I set 0 and 'unknown' rather than asserting a figure.",
