    vs_provider: "TradingView / eToro paid signal services and copy-trading platforms; quant signal desks",
    cost_saving_pct: 0,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "A live \"proof of edge\" trading-signal network run by DeltaCompute24. Miners commit encrypted directional trade calls (crypto, metals, forex) using a 2-hour drand timelock, with SHA256(signal) written on-chain via set_commitment; after the timelock opens, validators grade the plaintext against 1-minute candles \u2014 TP first = WON, SL first = LOST, neither by the horizon = WASH. Emissions go to miners whose Wilson lower-bound hit-rate beats 50%, with BASE/SHARP/WOLF tier multipliers (1x/1.2x/2x), a copy-detection penalty and a referral mechanism. Verifiably live today: the subnet is emitting (255,955 rao, 58 active miners, 5 validators, healthy epoch cadence), the site's Recruiters and Swarm boards were regenerating with fresh on-chain data at the time of research, a Telegram intake bot (@Iqsignals2026_bot) issues feed tokens, and an IQ Agent Chrome extension is published in the Chrome Web Store (ID hjjlcadipdpjjlomliokabacjimheebe). Two incentive mechanisms run under one netuid: low-frequency on-chain commits and a high-frequency WebSocket ingest with countersigned receipts Merkle-rooted on chain. Roadmap/thin: the \"Swarm\" is nine of the team's OWN accounts seeded at $5,000 each (~$45k total, 732 closed trades) with small and partly negative returns \u2014 it is a proprietary demo, not a customer product. Note SN89 is a full pivot: this netuid was previously \"InfiniteHash\" (a BTC pool / Lightning project, repo backend-developers-ltd/InfiniteHash), and the InfiniteQuant repo was only created 2026-06-06. AUDIT: Open source under MIT (DeltaCompute24/InfiniteQuant-Subnet), and the team is unusually candid about centralisation. docs/single-validator-model.md states plainly that SN89 deliberately runs ONE authoritative validator with other would-be validators child-keying/delegating to it, because multi-validator journal reconstruction failed in practice (~1 RPC/block historical-commitment access, and a second chain connection deadlocks substrate-interface). They describe the posture as \"centralized operation, decentralized verification\": trust is argued from replayability rather than redundancy, since every graded signal is an on-chain set_commitment hash signed by the miner's own hotkey at a consensus-exact block, grades are re-derivable from commit-block T0 plus public price feeds and committed bands, and the weight vector is a pure function of the journal (sn89_signals/replay.py). That materially limits weight fabrication but leaves clear single points of failure: one operator-run validator, an operator-run feed/token service (@Iqsignals2026_bot gates SN89_FEED_TOKEN), an operator-run HF WebSocket ingest, and Cloudflare R2 for checkpoint publication. The owner also sets the emission split between the LF and HF mechanisms on chain. No third-party security audit found. Contributor concentration is high: effectively two identities (DeltaCompute24 ~159 commits, whitdhamer ~12), 1 star, 0 forks. CAVEATS: Could not verify any paying customer, any revenue, or any usage number for the IQ Agent extension \u2014 the Chrome Web Store listing is JavaScript-rendered and install counts were not retrievable, so extension adoption is entirely unmeasured. No official project X account was found; the only x.com links on the site are individual trader handles being showcased (Coldie_Pips1, TOSIN_FX, Mahmoud6765, OkeQuadri43895), which are participants, not the project. On-chain discord field is empty and I found no Discord. A partner API host is referenced (partner.infinitequant.app/sn89/mechanisms) but returns {\"detail\":\"Not Found\"}, so any \"partner\" business line is unproven. The site's framing that the product is \"now live on the world's most powerful incentivized intelligence network\" is marketing; what is actually live is a subnet with 58 miners and 12 recruiters, of which only 2 recruiters and a handful of miners are actually earning \u2014 the Recruiters board itself showed 2/12 recruiters and 2/58 recruits scoring. The Swarm results are also being presented as validation of the signal quality, but they cover only days of trading on the team's own money and the currencies book was down ~2.6%; treat that as a demo, not evidence of edge. Finally, \"users\" here are emission-incentivised miners, not customers \u2014 I have deliberately not scored that as commercial traction.",
    active_users: "https://infinitequant.app/iq-agent \u2014 the only call-to-action is \"Add IQ Agent to Chrome\" with the fine print \"Free to install \u00b7 Pairs with the IQ Signals program\". There is no pricing page (https://infinitequant.app/pricing returns HTTP 404), no paid tier, no subscription and no invoicing surface anywhere on the site or in the public repo. The only money figures on the property are the team's own nine $5,000 prop-trading accounts on https://infinitequant.app/swarm, which are self-funded capital, not customer revenue. Miner emissions are Bittensor inflation, not revenue.",
