    vs_provider: "Azure/GCP confidential VMs with NVIDIA CC; Phala Network and Super Protocol on the decentralised side; Targon (SN4), Lium (SN51) and Chutes (SN64) inside Bittensor",
    cost_saving_pct: 0,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Confidential AI compute: GPU workloads run inside hardware TEEs (Intel TDX/SGX + NVIDIA Confidential Computing) using Kata Containers and Confidential Containers on RKE2/Rancher Kubernetes clusters, with Armada as the multi-cluster batch scheduler. Registered 2026-07-14, so roughly four weeks old. What is actually live, per the project's own honest \"What Ships Today\" table: the v1 Bittensor validator (a ~12-module Python container, 35 tests) which scores a single owner-operated staging cluster on an infrastructure-readiness gate and sets weights once per epoch; a USD-denominated pricing feed (Taostats TAO/USD + a Targon SN4 supply-side clamp) publishing a price card of H100 $3 / H200 $3.50 / B200 $6.50 / B300 $8 per GPU-hour; a LiteLLM gateway at llm.kubetee.ai serving GLM-5.2 and DeepSeek-V4-Flash on B200/H200; and an Albedo SN97 evaluation PoC that completed a 100-sample run on 2026-08-09. What is NOT live: Armada itself is not deployed, permissionless miner onboarding (the owner manually applies hotkey bindings), the 100 TAO miner deposit (measured, not enforced), the jobs MCP server, USDC-on-BASE billing, and paid jobs generally \u2014 customer payment is explicitly Phase 2. The live validator dashboard on 2026-08-12 shows exactly one miner (UID 56, the owner's own Oakland cluster, 16x B200 + 24x H200) earning $188/hr of a $1,446/hr pool, with 87% of emissions recycled. AUDIT: Everything in the stack is genuinely open source upstream (RKE2, Rancher, Kata, CoCo, Armada, LiteLLM, NVIDIA GPU Operator) and KubeTEE's own subnet repo is MIT with public forks of its patches \u2014 but the repo is 5 commits old, has 0 stars, and has exactly one contributor: Pierre A. Manseau (GitHub pamanseau, company \"KubeTEE AI LTD\", pierre@kubetee.ai). This is a one-person subnet, and that person is simultaneously the owner, the only validator operator of consequence, and the only miner. Miner onboarding is permissioned \u2014 KubeTEE applies the hotkey binding itself \u2014 so it is not an open network today. The validator runs on the operator's machine outside a TEE (running it inside an attested Kata/CoCo pod is an open roadmap item), which means the referee is currently unattested in a project whose entire pitch is attestation. The Taostats price feed is a hard dependency: if it fails the cycle is skipped. Credible security credentials: FIPS-140-2 validated RKE2 baseline (140-3 is a target, not held), NVIDIA Inception member, Confidential Computing Consortium member, upstream Kata/CoCo contributions. No third-party security audit of KubeTEE's own code exists. CAVEATS: The website in the on-chain identity, kubetee.ai, has no A record and does not resolve \u2014 there is no marketing site, only the LiteLLM subdomain and the GitHub README. That is a real red flag for a subnet claiming enterprise-grade AIaaS. Named partnerships are asserted but unverified by me: \"working directly with Intel and NVIDIA engineers\", the SN28/SayGM provider onboarding \"before Aug 15\", and FIPS-140-3 are all one-sided claims. The README is 80KB of specification for a network that currently has two active miner keys and one real cluster, so the gap between documented architecture and deployed reality is the largest of the four subnets here. The \"owner conviction auto-locked to perpetuity\" and $198k registration claims are unverified on-chain by me. No X account found.",
    active_users: "The project states it itself. https://github.com/KubeTEE-AI/kubetee-subnet README roadmap lists \"Alpha / TAO paid jobs (demand-side)\" as an unchecked Phase 0 item and puts \"USDC-on-BASE billing\" in Phase 2, and the \"What Ships Today\" table marks Payments as designed-not-built. The published $3-$8/GPU-hr card is a miner-scoring compensation target, not customer invoicing. The only miner being paid is the subnet owner's own cluster (https://s3.hippius.com/kubetee-validator/index.html).",
