    cost_saving_pct: 0,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Albedo is a trajectory-distillation, king-of-the-hill competition subnet. Miners distil a large teacher model into a smaller student (constraints previously published as <=33B total params, Kimi-family architecture, vocab 163,840), upload it to Hugging Face and commit the repo link on-chain; the validator runs duels on coding tasks, including SWE-bench-Verified style evaluation, and the winner takes the crown and the emissions. Every trace is published so the network progressively distils itself into better open checkpoints. Development is real and current - the repo has ~402 commits and commits on 2026-08-11 covering judge-leak fixes, prompt refactors, scoring artefacts and adding new inference providers - and the contributor set is the Dendrite team (dendrite-aprecat, tony-dendrite, dendrite-belps, weather-boss-dendrite) with commits from unconst, i.e. Bittensor co-founder Jacob Steeves. What does NOT exist: any website, product, API, docs site, pricing or customer-facing surface whatsoever. The subnet's output is open model checkpoints on Hugging Face, given away. AUDIT: Code is public and the mechanism is inspectable, which is the strongest thing here: 402 commits, five named contributors, active as of 11 Aug 2026, and the design deliberately publishes traces so scoring can be re-derived. The repo is real engineering, not a template fork. Against that: the repository sits under a personal account (unarbos) rather than an org, has no README, no licence file I could retrieve, and 2 stars - so there is no governance structure, no release process and nothing resembling institutional custody. The validator, the judge model and the remote GPU evaluators are operator-run; scoring depends on an LLM judge (one recent commit fixes a '<think> leak to judge'), which is a subjective, tamperable component sitting inside an otherwise objective duel. No third-party audit. Single point of failure: the same operator account also controls SN66 Conjectures tooling, SN3 Teutonic and the SN120 Affine repo, so SN97 is not an independent bet - it is one of four correlated positions on the same small team. CAVEATS: Could not verify: the on-chain subnet name is 'Albedo' per third-party listings and the repo description, but the same team's SN97 repo was called 'Distil' as recently as May 2026, so the name has already turned over once and may again. No X account, no Discord server, no website, no README - for a subnet at aGap rank 12 that is an unusually thin public footprint and the main reason I have not scored it higher despite genuine code activity. I could not confirm current miner count, whether any Albedo checkpoint is actually competitive on SWE-bench-Verified against public baselines, or whether the published traces are complete. I am raising the existing 40 only modestly, to 46: the engineering is credible and the team is top-tier, but there is no product, no user, no revenue and no public identity, and nothing here is buyable.",
    active_users: "There is no product to sell. No website exists (albedo.io is an unrelated parked domain that redirects to a registrar lander; albedo.ai and subnet97.ai do not resolve), no pricing, no API, no docs, no sponsor and no customer. The only artefacts are open Hugging Face checkpoints and public duel traces. Funding is entirely subnet emissions.",
    annual_revenue_usd: 0,
    revenue_confidence: "confirmed_pre_revenue",
    revenue_evidence: "There is no product to sell. No website exists (albedo.io is an unrelated parked domain that redirects to a registrar lander; albedo.ai and subnet97.ai do not resolve), no pricing, no API, no docs, no sponsor and no customer. The only artefacts are open Hugging Face checkpoints and public duel traces. Funding is entirely subnet emissions.",
