    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "MASX AI is a probabilistic forecasting engine run out of Essen, Germany, primarily by one engineer (Ateet Vatan). Two web platforms are genuinely live and publicly usable today: forecast.masxai.com, which publishes Brier-scored probability forecasts on conflicts, elections and macro events produced by a 'Council of Doctrines' of 35 agents, with resolved-forecast track-record and email briefing pages; and bt.masxai.com, a Bittensor-specific anomaly-detection dashboard covering emissions, dTAO liquidity, miner trajectories and validator behaviour across 50+ subnets, with Live Forecasts, Monitor, Proof, Explain, Methodology and Track Record sections. The subnet itself is much thinner than the websites. Its own README is titled 'MasXAI Subnet MVP': miners are Gemini-backed forecasting agents (GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-pro) that return a small JSON forecast schema, and the validator only issues event types listed in ENABLED_EVENT_TYPES \u2014 which by default is a single type, tao_price_movement, because it is the only one with an automatic oracle resolver. Five other event types (subnet_token_price, new_subnet_registration, governance_outcome, ecosystem_growth_metric, significant_bittensor_event) are defined but explicitly gated off pending resolvers, i.e. roadmap. On-chain: incentive_burn 0.953 (95% of miner incentive burned), 16 active miners, 2 active validators, market cap ~18,184 TAO. AUDIT: Code is open source under MIT at github.com/masxai/masxai-subnet, actively committed (last push 2026-08-12), but it is very young \u2014 created 2026-06-09 with only 3 contributors and 0 stars. The dominant committer, 'kattensor' (18 commits), is a GitHub account created 2026-06-21, i.e. a pseudonymous account opened specifically for this work; the identifiable human behind MASX is Ateet Vatan (github.com/AteetVatan), who describes himself as a solo LLM/automation architect. The companion masxai/masxai-docs repo is an untouched create-next-app template \u2014 the README is verbatim Next.js boilerplate \u2014 so there is no real subnet documentation site despite the on-chain identity implying one. Only 2 active validators means weight-setting is effectively controlled by one or two keys, and the operator has set 95% incentive burn, meaning the owner controls how much economic signal reaches miners. Miners depend on a single centralised third party (Google Gemini API) for their core inference, which is a hard external single point of failure. Owner coldkey 5HBb3F1bmDzdwQ5WTweXUvnKETTzu6aWNAH811vrLkvSdQAn, owner hotkey 5CoeuhimLNpjegk9zDBLmp9EBEy6X44Ad6naf2dCupkWYG6y. No third-party audit found. Key-person risk is severe: this is essentially one person. CAVEATS: I could not verify any of the headline numbers on masxai.com \u2014 '35 Doctrine Agents', '50+ Bittensor subnets monitored', '10 anomaly signal types', 'fully agentic, zero humans in the loop' are all self-asserted marketing with no third-party corroboration, and the site's Brier-score track-record pages are self-reported and self-scored. The gap between the polished marketing site ('Live \u00b7 Predictive intelligence engine', 'What enterprises do manually in months, MASX does autonomously in seconds') and the subnet's actual state (README self-labelled MVP, ONE enabled event type, 95% burn) is the single most important thing a buyer should notice \u2014 the enterprise framing is materially overstated relative to what ships. Web search and X API were unavailable this session, so I could not check @masxai posts, the LinkedIn company page, or podcasts for revenue or customer claims; a disclosed figure could exist there. Discord invite https://discord.gg/t8k9vm4KMG was not opened. This subnet had never been benchmarked, so there was no prior value to compare against.",
    active_users: "Both live platforms are explicitly free. The SoftwareApplication/WebApplication JSON-LD on https://forecast.masxai.com declares offers: {\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"0\",\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\"}. https://masxai.com/pricing returns HTTP 404 \u2014 there is no pricing page. The only conversion surface found is a free email-briefing subscribe page (https://forecast.masxai.com/subscribe). No paid tier, API key sales, enterprise plan, customer logos or funding announcement found anywhere on masxai.com, bt.masxai.com or forecast.masxai.com.",
    annual_revenue_usd: 0,
    revenue_confidence: "confirmed_pre_revenue",
    revenue_evidence: "Both live platforms are explicitly free. The SoftwareApplication/WebApplication JSON-LD on https://forecast.masxai.com declares offers: {\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"0\",\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\"}. https://masxai.com/pricing returns HTTP 404 \u2014 there is no pricing page. The only conversion surface found is a free email-briefing subscribe page (https://forecast.masxai.com/subscribe). No paid tier, API key sales, enterprise plan, customer logos or funding announcement found anywhere on masxai.com, bt.masxai.com or forecast.masxai.com.",
    last_updated: "2026-08-12",
    sources: ["https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/identity/v1?netuid=104", "https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/latest/v1?netuid=104", "https://api.taostats.io/api/dtao/pool/latest/v1", "https://masxai.com/", "https://masxai.com/pricing", "https://forecast.masxai.com/", "https://forecast.masxai.com/subscribe", "https://bt.masxai.com/", "https://bt.masxai.com/track-record", "https://github.com/masxai/masxai-subnet", "https://discord.gg/t8k9vm4KMG"],
