    benchmark_summary: "Finsight is a Canada-first personal investment intelligence platform at finsight.tech, with a live app at app.finsight.tech. It is split into a free tier and a paid-style tier. The free Portfolio Manager is described as \"free and live today\": TFSA/RRSP/Non-Registered accounts in one place, multi-currency (CAD/USD) holdings and transactions, watchlist, CRA-ready adjusted-cost-base tracking, and daily P&L/allocation/concentration snapshots. Everything AI-powered is not purchasable \u2014 the Pro tier (news scoring with sentiment, personalised newsroom, real-time quotes, AI co-pilot with bull/bear/BUY-HOLD-SELL reasoning, Black-Litterman rebalancing with Canadian tax warnings, smart alerts) is labelled \"Coming soon\", \"invite-gated\", behind an email waitlist with no price published. Two further items (Smith Maneuver tracker, Tax Optimization Suite) are explicitly roadmap. Declared data sources are Tiingo, Reddit, Google News, Marketaux and creator video. The differentiation is real and specific \u2014 superficial-loss checking across accounts before a trade, ACB with FX at settlement, account-aware rebalancing \u2014 but the monetizable layer is not yet open. AUDIT: Weakest area by far, and the reason the score is capped. There is no public code at all: the on-chain identity record has an empty github_repo field, and no Finsight subnet repo exists (github.com/finsight is an unrelated organisation hosting QUIKSharp, a .NET/Lua trading interface). That means the incentive mechanism, validator logic and miner interface for netuid 109 are entirely unauditable, and miners cannot inspect what they are being scored on. No Discord, no X account, no docs site (/docs, /pricing, /about and docs.finsight.tech all 404 \u2014 the site is a single page with anchors). The only contact is hello@finsight.tech. No third-party audit, no named team, no company registration disclosed. The product is a centralised SaaS on a private stack with a single operator \u2014 complete single point of failure, and the Bittensor layer is unverifiable from outside. To their credit, the site carries a clear disclaimer that nothing constitutes personalised financial, tax or legal advice and that AI views are model output, and it explicitly labels its screenshots \"All figures shown are illustrative and fictional\". CAVEATS: The most important flag: finsight.tech does not mention Bittensor, blockchain, subnets or decentralisation anywhere on the entire page, despite the on-chain description asserting \"Bittensor powers finsight.tech\". I could find no public evidence connecting the live web app to netuid 109's miners or validators \u2014 the subnet claim is unverified in both directions. I could not test the free Portfolio Manager: app.finsight.tech returns HTTP 200 but renders a client-side \"Loading\u2026\" shell behind a login, so \"free and live today\" is the company's claim, not something I confirmed. All dashboard numbers on the marketing site ($128,417.52 portfolio, 312 articles scored, etc.) are self-declared as fictional mockups, so they are worth nothing as traction evidence. I found zero social or press coverage of Finsight in a Bittensor context, no user counts, no funding. The score of 45 reflects a genuinely well-specified product with real Canadian-tax domain depth, discounted hard for zero open source, zero verifiable traction and no purchasable paid tier \u2014 do not read it as validation of the subnet mechanism, which I could not examine at all.",
    active_users: "https://finsight.tech/ pricing section \u2014 the only two tiers are \"Free \u00b7 Portfolio Manager\" (\"Portfolio Manager is free and live today\") and \"Coming soon \u00b7 Pro\", which has no price, no checkout and only an email capture: \"Invite-gated. No card, no spam \u2014 one email when your seat opens.\" There is no paid plan a customer can buy today, therefore no subscription revenue. No disclosed ARR, customer logos, user counts or funding announcement exists on the site or anywhere I could find.",
