    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Claims is a decentralised-science subnet that turns scientific papers into a structured claim-evidence graph: miners receive paper-extraction tasks and return structured claim-evidence packets, validators audit those outputs for source grounding, valid claim-evidence links and coverage of the task scope. The canonical pipeline is agent_v1, a skill-capable agent miner that mounts the ARA (Agent-Native-Research-Artifact) compiler skill from ARA-Labs \u2014 a substantial external project with 626 stars \u2014 and emits Claims-owned structured artifacts; a legacy v0 direct-extraction pipeline remains for backward compatibility. PDF ingestion runs through pdf-inspector by default with optional GROBID, and miners require an OPENROUTER_API_KEY. What is live today is the miner/validator software and 15 numbered design documents (schema, incentive mechanism, ontology linking, epistemic ontology, validator seal and benchmarks, roadmap-to-subnet); recent commits are adding DSPy Silver adjudication, concurrency limits and validator cost profiling. What is NOT live is any consumer or customer surface: there is no website (the on-chain subnet_url field is empty), no public API, no query interface, and no claim-evidence graph that a buyer can browse or license. Note this netuid previously hosted 'oneoneone', an unrelated UGC-scraping subnet \u2014 it has changed hands. On-chain: incentive_burn 1.0 (100% of miner incentive currently burned) with 1 active miner and 9 active validators, i.e. the incentive mechanism has not been switched on yet; market cap ~25,656 TAO with healthy two-way flow (179 buys vs 124 sells in 24h). AUDIT: Code is open source under MIT at github.com/DeSciClaims/Claims and is the most actively developed of the four \u2014 128 commits since the repo was created 2026-05-25, with commits landing daily through 2026-08-12. Design documentation is genuinely good: 15 numbered docs covering scoring, schema, incentive mechanism and validator seal, which is well above the Bittensor template baseline and is clearly original work, not a forked template. The serious weakness is bus factor: 128 of 129 commits are by a single developer, Ogban Ugot; the only other contributor is Philipp Koellinger with 1 commit. Koellinger's involvement is a real credibility signal \u2014 he is a known DeSci figure (philipp-koellinger.com) \u2014 but one commit is sponsorship, not engineering depth, and should not be read as an active team. The DeSciClaims org was created 2026-06-18, has zero public members, no blog and no listed email. Miners depend on OpenRouter (a centralised LLM router) and validators on the external ARA-Labs skill compiler \u2014 two third-party single points of failure. With 100% incentive burn the owner currently controls all economic signal. Owner coldkey 5Do2YQao1a5tPmcNyehkFq28y5G5uEX8fXjcrnCYbNc5mXJM, owner hotkey 5ExhNF86wqqBkyWwKRozATP8nRBUfyhVHKa7dquFchNRmaN5. No third-party audit found. CAVEATS: I could not verify the depth of Philipp Koellinger's or DeSci Labs' institutional backing \u2014 the GitHub link is real but I found no press release, funding announcement or DeSci Labs page confirming Claims as an official venture, and web search and X API were unavailable this session. Treat the DeSci association as suggestive, not established. I also could not verify miner output quality: with 100% incentive burn and 1 active miner there is no competitive network producing extractions yet, so all scoring and benchmark claims in the docs are untested at network scale. The Discord link in the on-chain identity is a channel inside the main Bittensor server, not a dedicated community, so community size is unmeasurable. There is a real risk this reads better on GitHub than it will in production \u2014 polished docs and a daily commit cadence from one developer are cheap relative to shipping a queryable graph, and the roadmap-to-subnet doc (0007) implies the network launch is still ahead. This subnet had never been benchmarked, so there was no prior value to compare against; note also that AlphaGap's stored record for netuid 111 still says 'oneoneone', which is stale and must be replaced.",
    active_users: "No commercial surface exists to generate revenue. The on-chain identity has an empty subnet_url and empty subnet_contact (https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/identity/v1?netuid=111). The GitHub repo homepage field is empty and the README documents only local miner/validator operation \u2014 no pricing, no API keys, no customers. Candidate domains desciclaims.org and claims.science do not resolve. The subnet is running 100% incentive burn with 1 active miner, so no production extraction work is being sold.",
