    subnet_name: "TensorUSD (TUSDT)",
    benchmark_score: 42,
    benchmark_category: "DeFi / Stablecoin",
    vs_provider: "Sky (MakerDAO) DAI, Liquity, Aave GHO",
    cost_saving_pct: 0,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "TensorUSD is a CDP-style overcollateralised stablecoin protocol native to Bittensor: users lock TAO (and subnet alpha) in a vault, mint TUSDT against it at a 150% collateralisation ratio, and are liquidated below a 120% ratio. The subnet itself is the decentralised liquidation and oracle layer \u2014 miners either bid in liquidation auctions (Mechanism 0, requires holding TUSDT plus a CoinMarketCap API key) or submit prediction agents that forecast vault health and minted supply one week out (Mechanism 1); validators track on-chain activity and set weights. This is the most build-complete of the four: ink! smart contracts (vault, auction, oracle, ERC-20 token, treasury, governance/election) are written and four mainnet contract addresses are published in the repo, plus a CLI, an SDK, a GitBook whitepaper v2, and a DAO subdomain. The fee model is explicit and live-documented: 10% interest fee and 11% liquidation fee. What is NOT live is usage. Their own homepage 'Live Protocol Data / real-time snapshot' panel reads $0.00 TUSDT minted, 0.00 TAO total value locked, 0 active vaults. So the machine is built and switched on, and nobody has used it. AUDIT: Fully open source and by far the most active development of the four: five public repos under the TensorUSD org, with commits landing on the day of research (2026-08-11), 100+ commits in the subnet repo and 100+ in the contract repo, and a genuine multi-contributor team (tao-chi, tensorusd09, yellow16b, benup211, Khem, coderNp101 \u2014 roughly 6 distinct identities). NOT a template fork. However: NO COMPLETED THIRD-PARTY AUDIT EXISTS. The homepage banner says only 'Smart contract audit underway with leading Web3 security firm'; a 'Bitsec' logo appears in the partner strip but I found no published audit report, no scope, and no date. For an overcollateralised stablecoin holding user TAO, that is the single most important gap. Centralisation risks a buyer must know: (1) the contract deployment README states 'the deployer becomes the initial governance of the vault, and (via instantiation) of the auction', with the subnet owner named as the initial 'maintainer' \u2014 so upgrade/governance authority sits with the founding keys until the election contract is actually handed over; (2) miners are instructed to use a CoinMarketCap API key for pricing, so the oracle depends on a centralised price source despite Pyth appearing in the partner strip; (3) app.tensorusd.com returns HTTP 401 (nginx basic auth), i.e. the application layer is still gated. Chain: 12 validators / 12 active, but only 1 active miner against 155 registered keys, meaning the liquidation and prediction mechanisms are effectively unstaffed. Subnet slot registered 2025-12-17. CAVEATS: BLUNT: the site's own claims outrun the evidence. 'MAINNET LIVE' and 'Real-time Audited' and 'Forever Stability... Users are guaranteed $1 value of $TUSDT forever' are overstated for a protocol with zero vaults, zero TVL and no completed audit \u2014 'Real-time Audited' in the docs refers to their own collateral-vault visibility, not to a security audit, and reads as deliberately ambiguous. 'No bank-run, No Death Spiral... 100% protected' is an unfalsifiable claim about an untested system. The roadmap has slipped badly: Q1 2026 items (legal review, contract verification, platform launch) were still pending in August 2026. Could not verify: whether the four published mainnet contract addresses hold any balance (I did not query them on-chain); the identity, jurisdiction or legal entity behind the '1:1 redeemable for US Dollar' claim, and no reserve attestation or banking partner is named anywhere \u2014 that claim should be treated as unsupported; the '500+ Discord members' figure; whether 'Ventura Labs' and 'Bitsec' are commercial engagements or logo placement. Never benchmarked before, so nothing to inherit; there is no stale prior figure to correct.",
    active_users: "https://tensorusd.com \u2014 the site's own 'Protocol Overview: a real-time snapshot of the protocol's on-chain health' block reads: '$0.00 $TUSDT Minted', 'Total Value Locked 0.00 TAO', 'Active Vaults 0', alongside 'Liquidation Fee 11%' and 'Interest Fee 10%'. Arithmetic: protocol revenue = 10% annual interest x $0 debt outstanding + 11% x $0 liquidated = $0. Corroborated by https://docs.tensorusd.com/roadmap-and-growth/roadmap, which still lists 'Paid subnet usage' / revenue validation as a Q3 2026 target and shows the Feb-Mar 2026 'platform launch' phase as still pending as of August 2026.",
