    benchmark_summary: "SOMA is run by Dendrite (Dendrite Quantum LTD, Limassol, Cyprus, HE 475409), an established Bittensor mining/infrastructure group that also operates on SN62 Ridges, SN17 404-GEN, SN6 Numinous, SN18 Zeus and SN57 Gaia. SOMA launched positioned as the 'first MCP-native subnet' \u2014 decentralised Model Context Protocol servers letting agents reach external tools \u2014 but as of Aug 2026 the working mechanism has narrowed to context and chain-of-thought compression: miners submit compression algorithms into two-week competition cycles (submission window, automated screening stage, then continuous validator scoring on SWE explore/edit tasks in sandboxes). Live and usable today: SOMARIZER, a free web demo that compresses a prompt, and an open-source context-compression plugin for OpenClaw (shipped 6 Aug 2026). Claimed results: 40.4% cheaper input tokens vs an uncompressed GPT-5.5 Pro prompt, and ~9% of all DeepSeek V4 Pro tokens routed through OpenRouter's DeepSeek provider in one week originating from SOMA evaluations. A packaged CLI tool promising 'up to 50% savings on AI costs' is on an early-access waitlist, i.e. roadmap. Cross-subnet MCP integrations remain 'coming soon'. The repo is real work \u2014 8 contributors, 220 PRs since Feb 2026, commits through 7 Aug 2026 \u2014 not a template fork. AUDIT: Open source under MIT (github.com/DendriteHQ/SOMA), 8 contributors including named Dendrite engineers, healthy PR-based workflow with dev/main branching and code review. Genuine positive signal on process: on 7 Aug 2026 Dendrite postponed their own Conviction Program to independently audit the relevant Subtensor lock code before asking holders to lock tokens \u2014 that is the correct instinct and rare. Against that: no third-party security audit of SOMA itself exists. Structural dependency risk is high \u2014 miners submit algorithms with OpenRouter API keys and evaluation runs on OpenRouter, so a centralised third party sits in the critical path of the incentive mechanism; validator sandboxes and the screening stage are operated to Dendrite's spec. Dendrite holds the subnet owner key and simultaneously runs miners/validators across at least five other subnets, so the same operator's capital and attention are spread thin and its stake gives it outsized influence here. The scoring mechanism is still being changed frequently (log2 compression ratios, magic-number fixes, 'evaluation variance fixes land next competition'), which means miner rewards are not yet stable. CAVEATS: Could NOT verify Dendrite's headline claims: '50+ elite engineers and mathematicians' (the SOMA repo shows 8 contributors), '150,000+ TAO generated since launch', or the btlabs_ai / Jose Rios partnership's substance beyond an announcement tweet. The '9% of DeepSeek V4 Pro tokens on OpenRouter' stat is genuinely interesting but is SOMA's own evaluation traffic \u2014 it measures how much compute the competition burns, not customer demand, and reading it as traction would be a mistake. The '40.4% cheaper' and 'up to 50% savings' figures are single self-run tests, not benchmarks, and no independent reproduction exists. The bigger strategic risk is positioning: SOMA was sold as the MCP subnet and has quietly become a prompt-compression subnet \u2014 the pitch and the product no longer match, and prompt compression is a thin, rapidly-commoditising layer that frontier labs are absorbing into native caching and context editing. Existing record's name and $0 revenue are both correct; the 58 score is roughly right and I have it at 60.",
    active_users: "Actively checked and found no monetisation of any kind: there is no pricing page, no paid tier, no checkout and no billing anywhere across dendrite.holdings, the SOMA GitHub, or the SOMA X account. Both shipped artefacts are given away free \u2014 SOMARIZER is a free demo and the OpenClaw compression plugin was open-sourced on 6 Aug 2026 (https://x.com/SomaSubnet/status/... 'The repository is live... now open source'). The only revenue-adjacent product, the SOMA CLI tool, is explicitly gated behind an early-access signup form as of 11 Aug 2026, i.e. not yet sold. Their own token 'Conviction Program' (a 50% bonus for locking SN114 tokens) is a tokenomics mechanic, not customer revenue, and was postponed on 7 Aug 2026 pending their own audit of Subtensor's conviction code.",
