    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. INACTIVE \u2014 parked, deregistered or abandoned.",
    benchmark_summary: "There is no product. HashiChain is a whitepaper abstract and nothing else. The stated concept is a sovereign Layer 1 for an 'agent economy' introducing a 'Probabilistic State Machine' that records intents rather than asset transfers, with miners as 'Solver Nodes' running AI models inside TEEs and a novel consensus primitive called 'Proof of Entanglement' that computes the probability of a semantic match between private agent intents, using Bittensor's Yuma consensus as the substrate. None of this is implemented. The entire repository consists of five files: .gitignore, LICENSE, a 2,240-byte README, a .DS_Store, and a 553KB logo image. There is no source code of any kind \u2014 GitHub reports no detected language for the repo. There is no miner implementation, no validator implementation, no protocol spec, no API, and no chain. Everything described above is roadmap; nothing is live. AUDIT: This is the clearest negative finding of the four and should be treated as a capital-preservation flag. The GitHub account hashi115 is a bare personal User account with no name, bio or blog, created 2025-12-08 \u2014 the same day the repository was created. The repo received five commits in a single 42-minute window on 2025-12-08 ('Initial commit' followed by four consecutive 'fix readme' commits) and has not been touched in the eight months since. It is the account's only repository. Contributors: one account plus a stray committer name 'zjp'. MIT licensed, but licensing an empty repo is meaningless. There is no code to audit, so open-source status is vacuous: nothing can be independently verified, no validator or miner logic is inspectable, and there is no way for anyone but the owner to know what, if anything, is being run. The subnet owner hotkey therefore constitutes a total single point of failure \u2014 the owner controls a registered netuid with no published mechanism whatsoever. Chain snapshot is consistent with an inactive shell: emission 0, only 1 active miner against 18 validators. No third-party audit, no named team, no legal entity, no contact beyond a free Outlook address (hashichain@outlook.com). The whitepaper's terminology ('Proof of Entanglement', 'Probabilistic State Machine', the 'Hashi' bridge-and-chopsticks metaphor) is unfalsifiable narrative with no accompanying formalism. CAVEATS: To be precise about what I could and could not establish: I confirmed the repository is code-free by listing its full git tree, and I confirmed the absence of a website by resolving the candidate domains directly \u2014 those are solid. What I could not do is rule out private development in an unlinked repository, or a rename to a project I have no thread to follow, since the on-chain identity record carries no website, Discord or X handle to trace. I also could not verify whether the netuid is still registered to the same owner as when the identity was set. Web search was unavailable this session, so I could not check whether HashiChain has any presence on Bittensor community forums, learnbittensor.org, subnetalpha.ai or crypto media \u2014 a search-based sweep could in principle surface something, though the total absence of contactable channels makes that unlikely. One caution on the chain reading: emission 0 is from a single point-in-time snapshot and could reflect a tempo artifact rather than a permanent state, so do not treat the zero as independently decisive \u2014 the empty repository is the load-bearing evidence, not the emission figure. On overstatement, essentially every claim in their own materials is overstated: calling itself 'The First Public Blockchain Designed for AI Agents' while shipping zero lines of code is the most straightforward instance. Treat the aGap rank 112 as generous.",
    active_users: "https://github.com/hashi115/hashichain \u2014 there is no product to monetise and no commercial surface of any kind: no website (the on-chain subnet_url field is empty, and hashichain.io and hashichain.ai both fail to resolve), no pricing page, no API, no signup, no Discord (the on-chain discord field is empty) and no X account (the on-chain twitter field is null). The repository contains only a README and a logo, with no source code. Revenue is definitionally zero.",
