    benchmark_summary: "There is no discoverable product. SN116 is a slot that was re-registered on 2026-05-30 (chain registration_block_number 8294730) and renamed from TaoLend to Memo on 2026-06-16. The previous occupant, TaoLend (a TAO lending protocol by xpenlab with a site at taolend.io and a repo at github.com/xpenlab/taolend), is gone; every third-party registry I checked still carries the stale TaoLend metadata because nothing has replaced it. The current on-chain subnet identity for netuid 116 contains the single field subnet_name = \"Memo\": no github_repo, no subnet_url, no contact, no discord, no logo, no summary, no tags, no twitter \u2014 every other field is empty or null. I found no website, no repository, no documentation, no API, no whitepaper and no team account anywhere. Chain state matches: 8 validators, 1 active miner out of 207 active keys, emission 0 in the snapshot I pulled, and incentive_burn set to 1.0, meaning 100% of miner incentive is burned. Alpha does trade and is volatile (+683.9% in a week around 2026-06-01, then -79.9% the week of 2026-07-27), but price action is the only activity I can evidence. AUDIT: Unauditable, and that is the finding. No public repository exists for the current project, so there is no code to review, no licence, no commit history and no contributor set. github.com/xpenlab/taolend, which metagraph.sh and tensorplex-labs/subnet-docs still list as the SN116 source repo, belongs to the deregistered predecessor and is not evidence about Memo. No third-party audit. The subnet is a total single point of failure: one owner coldkey (5F48aA3Pw1vFRfnhhfu7EJKqzrj8y9VBWtS4PE9xJ1chHXqB) and owner hotkey (5CXN6pP6ing9qguYEqtPLB5pphxAKpYabVe7uvLSysENsub5), a single active miner, and an incentive_burn of 1.0 that routes miner incentive to burn rather than to work. Two independent community allegations a buyer must be aware of, both from X and both unverified by me: taoleeh on 2026-07-12 \u2014 \"SN116 ('Memo') is actively exploiting and stealing from #Bittensor\"; and TAOTemplar on 2026-07-29 \u2014 \"Memo (Bittensor subnet #sn116) Subnet owner dumped.\" I could not obtain an owner response to either because there is no team account, site or Discord to check. CAVEATS: Be blunt about what this is: a renamed, unidentified slot with no product, no code and no public team, trading on volatility. The supplied name \"Memo\" is correct as the current on-chain name but conveys nothing \u2014 there is no evidence it refers to a memory/notes product or to anything at all. What I could not verify: who the owner is, whether any development exists privately, whether \"Memo\" is a pre-announcement placeholder for something real, and whether the two allegations above are accurate \u2014 they are third-party X posts, not proof, and I found no primary evidence of an exploit mechanism. I also could not fully separate the 2026-05-30 registration event from the 2026-06-16 rename; both are consistent with the slot changing hands, and the +567% price move on 2026-05-30 coincides with the registration. My emission = 0 reading is a single snapshot at block ~8,830,49x and could be an epoch-boundary artefact rather than a permanently gated emission; the 1 active miner and 100% incentive burn are the more robust signals. I am scoring this below 30 and marking it inactive on product grounds, not on trading grounds \u2014 the alpha token is liquid, the subnet as a product is not there.",
    active_users: "No product surface of any kind exists to generate revenue. On-chain identity for netuid 116 (https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/identity/v1) returns only {\"netuid\":116,\"subnet_name\":\"Memo\"} with github_repo, subnet_url, subnet_contact, discord, summary, description and twitter all empty or null. Chain state at https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/latest/v1?netuid=116 shows active_miners = 1, validators = 8, emission = 0, incentive_burn = 1.0 (full burn of miner incentive). No website, API, pricing page, repo or docs could be located despite searching the chain identity, taostats, metagraph.sh registry, tensorplex-labs/subnet-docs, GitHub org/repo/code search and X.",
