    vs_provider: "None (research prize; nearest analogue is the academic Hutter Prize)",
    cost_saving_pct: 0,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Glyph is a lossless neural text-compression benchmark subnet on netuid 117 \u2014 the team describes it as a perpetual, decentralised Hutter Prize. Miners commit one permanent codec per hotkey; validators sample fresh, never-before-seen text and run each codec's compress-then-decompress round trip in local Docker on an RTX 4090 (with Chutes/SN64 serverless GPU as an optional secondary path). Score is compression ratio, compressed divided by raw, gated on a hard bit-exact round-trip requirement, and weights are set king-of-the-hill: a challenger takes the crown only by beating the incumbent by a 1% epsilon threshold, and emission follows measured improvement rather than slot position (15% of the pot per 1% of ratio improvement over the dethroned winner, plus a one-off 25% base for the current leader). There is also a 10% temporal burn to UID 0 and a 'Miner Conviction' rule requiring winners to chain-lock cumulative alpha earnings to their hotkey. Critically, this is a research prize mechanism, not a product: there is no API, no pricing, no customers and nothing for sale. Glyph took over the netuid 117 slot from the previous occupant BrainPlay (a Shiftlayer LLC game-based LLM benchmark) around mid-2026. AUDIT: Open source at github.com/glyph-research/glyph-subnet (non-fork, created 2026-06-16, CI configured with pinned ruff for reproducible lint). Subnet owner coldkey 5HdThE9WvusfeFpk7R3Lnc9wfP4zsDje3GeRew6mrQHNNFiY. No third-party audit. The decentralisation posture is the weakest of the four by a wide margin and a buyer must understand this: on-chain the subnet is close to empty, with only 2 active validators, 1 active miner and 127 registered keys, against emission of just 72,934 \u2014 roughly 4% of subnet 124's and about 2.7% of subnet 102's. A single active miner means the king-of-the-hill ladder currently has effectively no competition. Contributor concentration is extreme: meowjet has 176 commits versus phplaboratory at 11 and vibecycle at 1, so bus-factor is 1. The reward mechanism is unusually owner-controlled and was materially rewritten recently \u2014 the epsilon threshold was cut from 5% to 1% and reward distribution switched to dynamic in version 1.3.0 (issue #177, 2026-07-24) \u2014 and the burn is toggled by a constant in the codebase (core.constants.BURN_ENABLED), meaning the owner can switch emission burn on or off unilaterally. Validation depending on a specific consumer GPU (RTX 4090) also limits who can realistically validate. CAVEATS: The aGap-supplied name 'glyph' is correct and current, but note the prior benchmark data for netuid 117 is worthless \u2014 the slot previously ran BrainPlay by Shiftlayer LLC, whose repo is a fork, has only 2 stars, 13 open issues and has been stale since 2026-04-20. Do not carry any BrainPlay history forward. I could not load docs.glyph-research.org (connection failed), so the deeper technical documentation is unverified. There is a factual discrepancy I could not resolve in the project's favour: the website summary describes compressing text 'while maintaining semantic meaning for downstream AI systems', which implies lossy semantic compression, whereas the README specifies strictly lossless with a hard bit-exact round-trip gate \u2014 I trust the README, and the website framing is loose at best. The site's leaderboard claims 64 validators and a 14x average compression ratio, which flatly contradicts the on-chain reading of 2 active validators; I could not reconcile this and consider the site's numbers unreliable. Social presence is essentially nil \u2014 the @glyphresearch X account has posted only twice ever (2026-07-09 and 2026-07-17), both bare links. Repo has 0 stars and last push was 2026-07-30, about two weeks stale. This is a competent single-developer research project with almost no network participation, and it is scored accordingly.",
    active_users: "https://glyph-research.org/ and https://github.com/glyph-research/glyph-subnet \u2014 the entire published mechanism is a compression benchmark paying miners in subnet emissions. There is no pricing page, no API, no commercial offering, no customers, and no monetisation section anywhere in the site or the README; the site's only economic figures are TAO emissions (e.g. daily emissions to top performers). Grepping the README for pricing, revenue, enterprise, customer, paid, subscription and commercial terms returned no commercial hits. This is a pre-revenue research subnet by design.",
    annual_revenue_usd: 0,
    revenue_confidence: "confirmed_pre_revenue",
    revenue_evidence: "https://glyph-research.org/ and https://github.com/glyph-research/glyph-subnet \u2014 the entire published mechanism is a compression benchmark paying miners in subnet emissions. There is no pricing page, no API, no commercial offering, no customers, and no monetisation section anywhere in the site or the README; the site's only economic figures are TAO emissions (e.g. daily emissions to top performers). Grepping the README for pricing, revenue, enterprise, customer, paid, subscription and commercial terms returned no commercial hits. This is a pre-revenue research subnet by design.",
    last_updated: "2026-08-12",
    sources: ["https://glyph-research.org/", "https://github.com/glyph-research/glyph-subnet", "https://api.github.com/repos/glyph-research/glyph-subnet", "https://api.github.com/repos/glyph-research/glyph-subnet/contributors", "https://api.github.com/repos/glyph-research/glyph-subnet/commits", "https://api.github.com/repos/glyph-research/glyph-subnet/readme", "https://taostats.io/subnets/117", "https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/latest/v1?netuid=117", "https://api.github.com/repos/shiftlayer-llc/brainplay-subnet", "https://x.com/glyphresearch"],
