    benchmark_summary: "On-chain identity describes Satori as building a persistent \"Second Life\" in Japan \u2014 AI companions with a day/night cycle that autonomously \"explore\" real Japanese landmarks by day and hold personal conversations at night, with emotional bonds mapped to real-world value via \"Digital Residency\" and cultural souvenirs. None of that is verifiable as a product. Nothing is live: the GitHub repository declared on chain (Satori119/Satori) returns 404 and the GitHub account Satori119 has zero public repositories, so the logo_url the subnet publishes is also a dead link. There is no website (the on-chain subnet_url field is empty), no Discord, no X account, and the only contact is a personal Outlook address (Akihabara119@outlook.com). On chain the subnet is inert: emission is 0 with just 1 active miner against a 256-neuron cap. There is no product, no API, no docs and no code to evaluate \u2014 this is a registered netuid with a concept description attached, not a working system. Treat the AI-companion narrative as an unbuilt pitch. AUDIT: Nothing to audit. No public source code at all \u2014 the only declared repository does not exist and the owning GitHub account has published nothing since it was created on 2025-10-17. No license, no documentation, no third-party audit, no disclosed team, and an anonymous free-webmail contact address. The owner coldkey is 5GbLENPLG8Takn1puaz5HorPmrFtDT7i2PojiJsqutbaGwWu; with 10 validators registered but only 1 active miner and zero emission, whatever weight-setting exists is entirely unobservable and unverifiable from outside. The project is a total single point of failure: one anonymous operator, no code, no infrastructure anyone can inspect. A buyer should treat this as an unaccountable shell. CAVEATS: I could not establish who is behind this at all \u2014 no team names, no company, no funding, no social presence. It is possible the team is developing privately and simply has not published, but there is zero external evidence of any build, so I am scoring only what is verifiable. I also could not determine whether the subnet was ever functional and has since decayed, or was never built; the GitHub account's last profile update was 2026-03-25, which is the most recent sign of life I found anywhere. Note that AlphaGap's own tao-pages copy currently describes SN119 as a real-time streaming-data intelligence product competing with Kafka/Kinesis \u2014 that description does not match the on-chain identity at all and appears to be wrong; it should be corrected or removed. My earlier cached DB row also carried the correct AI-companion description, so the streaming-data copy is the outlier.",
    active_users: "There is no product surface that could take money: the declared repo https://github.com/Satori119/Satori is 404, the GitHub user https://github.com/Satori119 shows public_repos: 0, the on-chain subnet_url and discord fields are empty strings, and chain state shows emission 0 with 1 active miner (https://api.taostats.io/api/subnet/latest/v1?netuid=119). No pricing page, app, storefront or paid tier exists to be found.",
