    subnet_name: "Affine",
    benchmark_score: 62,
    benchmark_category: "AI Model Training / Reinforcement Learning",
    vs_provider: "OpenAI, DeepSeek, Meta Llama and other frontier labs' open-weight releases; Prime Intellect and Nous Research on the decentralised-training side",
    cost_saving_pct: 70,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Affine is a competitive model-training subnet founded by Jacob Steeves (Const, Bittensor co-founder) under the Affine Foundation. Miners submit model checkpoints; validators run them against verifiable RL/reasoning environments and award emissions to whichever model wins. The live affine.io dashboard shows the current mechanism is a king-of-the-hill duel contract - 'Reason' score, paired z-margin versus the reigning king with a 2-sigma dethrone threshold and a delta=0.002 crown floor, plus a live duel queue, reign history and registration-burn chart - and the GitHub description now reads 'teacher-anchored distillation subnet (validator, evalsrv, research harness)', i.e. the original Pareto-frontier multi-environment design has already been replaced. Outputs are given away: the site publishes an open dataset and an llms.txt, and winning models have historically been hosted for public inference via Chutes (SN64). There is no product to purchase, no API key, no pricing and no customer-facing surface - the buyer of Affine's output today is the open-source community, for free. AUDIT: Mechanism is transparent and adversarially designed - the duel contract, dethrone margin and score history are published live, and the model artefacts and datasets are open, which makes the competition itself auditable. But the code posture is a genuine red flag: the AffineFoundation org has exactly one public repo, created 2026-08-04, with 0 stars and a single contributor ('unarbos' / Arbos) responsible for all ~2,341 commits, at a rate of roughly 290 commits/day with agent-style messages ('mining p2254: warm-arm R27 BigG-GRPO...'). The previously-cited repo AffineFoundation/affine-cortex now 404s, so the prior codebase and its history are gone. Validator operation, the evaluation server and the GPU evaluators are operator-run; there is no independent validator implementation. No third-party audit. Single points of failure: one maintainer holding the weight-version contract (affine/affine.toml, weight_version_key=3), and dependence on external hosting (Chutes/SN64) for serving. Notably the same operator account also runs SN97 Albedo and SN3 Teutonic and Const (unconst) commits into the Albedo repo, so SN120 and SN97 are effectively the same team running near-identical distillation king-of-the-hill mechanisms - a correlation risk if you hold both. CAVEATS: The existing benchmark of 78 is not supportable and I have cut it. Affine's strength is emissions rank and founder pedigree, neither of which is product traction: there is no disclosed customer, no revenue, and the output is free. Could not verify: the claim that top models remain hosted on Chutes for public inference (I found no live endpoint), any inference volume, contributor headcount beyond one public account, or the legal status of the 'Affine Foundation'. Overstated in circulating material: 'miners earning thousands of dollars daily' is emissions redistribution, not economic demand, and describing Affine as 'an infrastructure layer that coordinates multiple AI subnets' is aspirational - what is running is a single duel loop. The 2026-08-04 repo wipe and the mid-flight mechanism change from Pareto-frontier RL to teacher-anchored distillation both happened inside the last two weeks, so any thesis older than that is stale.",
    active_users: "No pricing page, paywall, API billing, sponsor or customer exists on affine.io or in the AffineFoundation/affine repository; the site's only calls to action are 'Dataset', 'Metrics' and 'llms.txt', all free. Monetisation is emissions-funded: miners are paid in subnet alpha and the artefacts are released openly. Third-party write-ups (simplytao.ai, subnetalpha.ai) describe reward flows to miners only and disclose no external revenue.",
