    subnet_id: 124,
    subnet_name: "Swarm",
    benchmark_score: 74,
    benchmark_category: "Robotics / Autonomy",
    vs_provider: "Skydio / Shield AI (closed-source drone autonomy stacks)",
    cost_saving_pct: 0,
    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. Active.",
    benchmark_summary: "Swarm is an open benchmark arena for autonomous drone-flight AI on Bittensor subnet 124. Validators procedurally generate fresh, never-before-seen 3D worlds and run miner-submitted pre-trained reinforcement-learning control policies inside headless dockerised PyBullet physics simulations, scoring them on task success and speed. What is live today: five distinct mission families (Interceptor, search-and-rescue and others), roughly 1,100 fresh worlds generated per week, 60-second flight evaluations, a public leaderboard at swarm124.com/benchmark, and released open-source artefacts including SOTApilot (a claimed 95.34% success state-of-the-art navigation stack), an open Tello-drone interceptor with YOLO detection plus Kalman tracking, and Langostino (a ROS2 autonomous drone platform, the org's most-starred repo at 175 stars). The buyer today is nobody in cash terms: miners are paid in subnet emissions, and the leaderboard is free and public. Commercial motion is nascent \u2014 the team publicly offers bespoke interceptor builds via its own lab and has run real-world field tests with DJI drones alongside MEVIDRONS at the Grandvalira ski resort, but no customer contract has been disclosed. Roadmap/expansion (announced 2026-07-16) is multi-drone swarm coordination and high-speed autonomous interception. AUDIT: Fully open source (github.com/swarm-subnet/swarm, non-fork, Apache-style public repo) and the evaluation harness is public, which is the main trust anchor \u2014 anyone can inspect how policies are scored. Subnet owner coldkey 5HKYqfJrUFKYPMRFZZ7kfhUNEyHUbY2ZyEjQqKJf2RKVpeXM. On-chain state is healthy relative to peers: 13 active validators, 23 active miners, 256 registered keys, emission 1,823,157. No third-party security audit found, and none would be especially meaningful for a simulation-benchmark subnet. Key centralisation risks a buyer should know: (a) contributor concentration \u2014 4 contributors total but 2 accounts (S3333F 594 commits, miguelik2 352) do essentially all work, so bus-factor is roughly 2; (b) validators run miner-submitted code in Docker on their own hardware, so sandbox escape is the standing attack surface; (c) scoring depends on the team's procedural world generator and benchmark calibration, which the owner controls \u2014 recent commits ('benchmark calibration', 'Calibrate the host before the benchmark workers start', 2026-08-08/10) show scoring parameters are actively tuned by the core team, giving the owner meaningful discretion over reward distribution. CAVEATS: Could not verify any of the commercial claims. The 95.34% SOTApilot figure is self-reported on their own benchmark \u2014 they define the test set, so it is not an independent result. The Grandvalira/DJI/MEVIDRONS field tests are described in their own tweets only; I found no counterparty confirmation and no indication they were paid engagements rather than demos. 'Real-world drone deployment' is the overstated claim on their materials \u2014 everything verifiable is simulation plus small Tello/DJI proof-of-concept flights, not production drone operations. swarm124.com is a JavaScript app I could not render, so I could not inspect the live leaderboard or confirm current miner counts from the site itself. Note also that only 23 of 256 registered keys are active miners.",
    active_users: "No disclosed revenue figure found anywhere. Two items that look like revenue but are NOT: (1) a 1,000 TAO 'strategic investment' from @Ever_BlueGreen announced 2026-03-18 \u2014 that is investment/pool commitment, not revenue; (2) '$2M locked in conviction' cited in their 2026-06-24 anniversary post \u2014 that is miner alpha locked on-chain, not customer payment. They do advertise paid custom builds ('Need one customized for your use case? Our lab can build it in weeks', 2026-07-28), so I cannot assert zero revenue, but I found no evidence of any paid engagement. Hence unknown rather than confirmed_pre_revenue.",
