    perf_delta: "Researched 2026-08-12. INACTIVE \u2014 parked, deregistered or abandoned.",
    benchmark_summary: "8 Ball has no product. Its on-chain identity record contains a name and nothing else \u2014 description, website, GitHub, Discord, Twitter and logo are all empty. The only substantive information available is community reporting from Sept\u2013Nov 2025 attributing it to @Barbarian7676 (owner of MANTIS, SN123) and describing an intended \"first prediction market powered by Bittensor\" \u2014 an on-chain Polymarket/Kalshi where miners would facilitate individual transactions, with an incentive mechanism said to be based on a whitepaper from @neuromancer_t of Sportstensor (SN41). Nothing was ever launched publicly. The founder was already being asked for updates in Oct 2025 (\"SN123 and SN125, both promising projects, but the only real issue remains communication\"), and his entire 2026 output \u2014 TRADEMIX v2, XSEC-RANK audits, June buyback-and-burn, incentive-mechanism upgrades \u2014 concerns MANTIS/SN123 exclusively. No mention of 8 Ball by anyone in 2026. There is no repo, no docs, no app, no testnet, no pricing. AUDIT: Nothing to audit \u2014 this is the worst possible posture. No open-source code has ever been published, so the incentive mechanism, validator logic and any funds handling are entirely unverifiable. No Discord, no website, no contact address, no docs. The subnet owner coldkey is 5DTzv2rL6YGQjCDNiWQJz2nE23fK1mDccH9eQimgiieyL3C4, which is a different key from the SN123/MANTIS owner (5HVuEdEGMYisecwjkWC7dKDPEzgs9cECdsdCQagfPRVf6FxZ), so the Barbarian attribution rests on community reporting rather than on-chain linkage. For a product category that would custody or settle user bets, the complete absence of code, audit or disclosed operators is disqualifying. Single point of failure is total: one anonymous owner key and no published anything. CAVEATS: The 8 Ball attribution to @Barbarian7676 comes from third-party community accounts (@CryptoZPunisher, @Pop_Collapse) in Sept\u2013Nov 2025, not from a first-party announcement I could open, and the owner coldkey does not match MANTIS's. I could not find a single first-party statement from the SN125 team, in any channel, ever. I could not rule out that the slot has been quietly repurposed or resold since \u2014 the chain still shows 256 registered keys and 15 active validators, so the netuid is populated, but there is no evidence any of that activity corresponds to a prediction market. Treat the \"prediction market\" description as a 2025 stated intention, not a current roadmap. Anyone modelling this should treat it as a name on a registry, not a project.",
    active_users: "No product exists to generate revenue: the on-chain identity for netuid 125 carries empty description, subnet_url, github_repo, discord and twitter fields, and no launched prediction market, app, API or pricing page could be found anywhere. The named founder's 2026 public updates cover only SN123/MANTIS (including a stated ~$12,000 June buyback-and-burn for MANTIS, not for SN125).",
